475\n342\t      - 28\n343\t      - -0.02\n344\t      - 0.93\n345\t      - noisy flat\n346\t    - - te\n347\t      - LOW\n348\t      - 0.502\n349\t      - 36\n350\t      - -0.18\n351\t      - 0.4\n352\t      - n.s.\n353\t    - - my\n354\t      - LOW\n355\t      - 0.468\n356\t      - 32\n357\t      - 0.1\n358\t      - 0.64\n359\t      - non-monotonic\n360\t  - name: 'Table 1b: Qwen3-235B Transfer Conditions Summary (20 langs, EN-optimal\n361\t      layer)'\n362\t    columns:\n363\t    - condition\n364\t    - mean_auroc\n365\t    - std\n366\t    - delta_vs_zs\n367\t    - significant_improvement_count\n368\t    rows:\n369\t    - - zero-shot\n370\t      - 0.576\n371\t      - 0.068\n372\t      - —\n373\t      - —\n374\t    - - mean-shift\n375\t      - 0.576\n376\t      - 0.068\n377\t      - 0.0\n378\t      - 0/20\n379\t    - - linear_proj_200\n380\t      - 0.612\n381\t      - 0.055\n382\t      - 0.036\n383\t      - 11/20\n384\t    - - fewshot_25\n385\t      - 0.598\n386\t      - 0.061\n387\t      - 0.022\n388\t      - 7/20\n389\t    - - fewshot_100\n390\t      - 0.625\n391\t      - 0.049\n392\t      - 0.049\n393\t      - 13/20\n394\t  figures_description:\n395\t  - 'Figure 1a: EN AUROC vs best ZS AUROC scatter across 24 layers for Qwen3-235B,\n396\t    colored by resource tier. Diffuse cloud without clean Pareto frontier. Non-monotonic\n397\t    language trajectories (ja, ko, am, my) highlighted. Annotation: global ρ=-0.12\n398\t    (p=0.078).\n399\t\n400\t    '\n401\t  - 'Figure 1b: ZS AUROC heatmap (language × probed layer). Irregular MoE-specific\n402\t    layer-to-layer variance, no smooth depth gradient. Expert routing artifacts visible\n403\t    as 4-layer-period oscillations.\n404\t\n405\t    '\n406\t  analysis: 'Qwen3-235B 的 Pareto frontier 远不如 Qwen2.5-7B pilot 清晰。MoE expert routing\n407\t    打破了 dense model 中 depth = specialization 的单调映射。Pilot 的 clear Pareto（L27 EN best\n408\t    但 transfer drops 2-4pp vs L24）是 dense 7B model 的特殊现象。仅 1/20 语言达到 per-language\n409\t    显著性（hi），且部分语言方向反转——depth-transfer tradeoff 不是普遍现象。对 Claim 1 构成 严重挑战：不能声称 Qwen\n410\t    系列存在 consistent Pareto。\n411\t\n412\t    '\n413\t- name: Llama 4 Scout Full Pareto Frontier\n414\t  plan_id: plan_002\n415\t  description: 'Llama 4 Scout (48 layers, 17B-16E MoE, W4A16), 12 probed layers (every\n416\t    4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions.\n417\t\n418\t    '\n419\t  expected_results:\n420\t    en_best_auroc: 0.718\n421\t    en_best_layer: 40\n422\t    en_auroc_range:\n423\t    - 0.615\n424\t    - 0.718\n425\t    en_best_ece_raw: 0.215\n426\t    zs_pass_count_auroc_gt_058: 9\n427\t    zs_pass_rate: 0.45\n428\t    mean_zs_auroc_all_20: 0.562\n429\t    mean_zs_auroc_drop_vs_en_pp: 15.6\n430\t    best_zs_auroc:\n431\t      zh: 0.648\n432\t      es: 0.655\n433\t      fr: 0.642\n434\t      de: 0.635\n435\t      ja: 0.562\n436\t      pt: 0.648\n437\t      it: 0.631\n438\t      ar: 0.588\n439\t      hi: 0.548\n440\t      ru: 0.608\n441\t      ko: 0.575\n442\t      tr: 0.531\n443\t      vi: 0.558\n444\t      th: 0.515\n445\t      sw: 0.501\n446\t      bn: 0.508\n447\t      am: 0.472\n448\t      yo: 0.458\n449\t      te: 0.491\n450\t      my: 0.452\n451\t    global_spearman_rho_depth_vs_transfer: -0.06\n452\t    global_spearman_p: 0.31\n453\t    per_lang_significant_negative_rho_count: 0\n454\t    per_lang_significant_positive_rho_count: 0\n455\t    per_lang_nonmonotonic_count: 8\n456\t    pareto_tradeoff_prevalence: 0.05\n457\t    pareto_depth_transfer_drop_final_layers_pp: 0.3\n458\t    mean_shift_delta_auroc_all: 0.0\n459\t    transfer_conditions_summary:\n460\t      zero_shot:\n461\t        mean_auroc: 0.562\n462\t        std: 0.065\n463\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n464\t      mean_shift:\n465\t        mean_auroc: 0.562\n466\t        std: 0.065\n467\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n468\t      linear_proj_200:\n469\t        mean_auroc: 0.598\n470\t        std: 0.052\n471\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.036\n472\t      fewshot_25:\n473\t        mean_auroc: 0.584\n474\t        std: 0.058\n475\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.022\n476\t      fewshot_100:\n477\t        mean_auroc: 0.611\n478\t        std: 0.048\n479\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.049\n480\t  result_rationale: 'Llama 4 Scout EN best AUROC 0.718 在 worst 范围低端——active parameters\n481\t    17B 但 16 experts 的稀疏激活使得每个 token 实际使用的参数量有限，correctness signal 在 expert 间被稀释。W4A16\n482\t    量化额外损耗 ~0.5-1pp。\n483\t\n484\t    ZS pass 9/20 (45%)，比 Qwen3 低因为：(1) Llama 4 Scout 的 multilingual pretraining 比例可能低于\n485\t    Qwen3（Qwen 系列历来强调多语言）；(2) 16-expert MoE 的 expert specialization 程度更高，语言间 representation\n486\t    divergence 更大。MVP 中 Llama-3.1-8B dense 的 5/5 pass 不推广——8B dense → Scout MoE 的架构变化比\n487\t    scale change 更根本。\n488\t\n489\t    Global Pareto rho=-0.06 (p=0.31) 完全不显著，0/20 语言 per-language 显著。仅 12 probed layers\n490\t    使 per-language Spearman 功效极低（n=12），但即使考虑 power 问题，effect sizes 也很小 （max |rho|\n491\t    = 0.38）。Scout 的 expert routing 比 Qwen3 更激进（16 experts vs Qwen3 的 设计），导致 depth-transfer\n492\t    关系更加 noisy。\n493\t\n494\t    Final-layer drop 仅 0.3pp——transfer 在 L40-L48 区间几乎 flat，没有 tradeoff 可言。\n495\t\n496\t    '\n497\t  tables:\n498\t  - name: 'Table 2a: Llama 4 Scout Per-Language Pareto Spearman ρ'\n499\t    columns:\n500\t    - lang\n501\t    - tier\n502\t    - best_zs_auroc\n503\t    - spearman_rho\n504\t    - p_value\n505\t    rows:\n506\t    - - zh\n507\t      - HIGH\n508\t      - 0.648\n509\t      - -0.18\n510\t      - 0.58\n511\t    - - es\n512\t      - HIGH\n513\t      - 0.655\n514\t      - -0.12\n515\t      - 0.71\n516\t    - - fr\n517\t      - HIGH\n518\t      - 0.642\n519\t      - -0.22\n520\t      - 0.49\n521\t    - - de\n522\t      - HIGH\n523\t      - 0.635\n524\t      - -0.08\n525\t      - 0.81\n526\t    - - ja\n527\t      - HIGH\n528\t      - 0.562\n529\t      - 0.32\n530\t      - 0.31\n531\t    - - pt\n532\t      - HIGH\n533\t      - 0.648\n534\t      - -0.15\n535\t      - 0.64\n536\t    - - it\n537\t      - HIGH\n538\t      - 0.631\n539\t      - -0.05\n540\t      - 0.88\n541\t    - - ar\n542\t      - MID\n543\t      - 0.588\n544\t      - 0.22\n545\t      - 0.49\n546\t    - - hi\n547\t      - MID\n548\t      - 0.548\n549\t      - -0.38\n550\t      - 0.22\n551\t    - - ru\n552\t      - MID\n553\t      - 0.608\n554\t      - -0.02\n555\t      - 0.95\n556\t    - - ko\n557\t      - MID\n558\t      - 0.575\n559\t      - 0.35\n560\t      - 0.26\n561\t    - - tr\n562\t      - MID\n563\t      - 0.531\n564\t      - 0.08\n565\t      - 0.81\n566\t    - - vi\n567\t      - MID\n568\t      - 0.558\n569\t      - 0.12\n570\t      - 0.71\n571\t    - - th\n572\t      - MID\n573\t      - 0.515\n574\t      - -0.18\n575\t      - 0.58\n576\t    - - sw\n577\t      - LOW\n578\t      - 0.501\n579\t      - -0.25\n580\t      - 0.43\n581\t    - - bn\n582\t      - LOW\n583\t      - 0.508\n584\t      - -0.08\n585\t      - 0.81\n586\t    - - am\n587\t      - LOW\n588\t      - 0.472\n589\t      - 0.02\n590\t      - 0.95\n591\t    - - yo\n592\t      - LOW\n593\t      - 0.458\n594\t      - -0.12\n595\t      - 0.71\n596\t    - - te\n597\t      - LOW\n598\t      - 0.491\n599\t      - -0.05\n600\t      - 0.88\n601\t    - - my\n602\t      - LOW\n603\t      - 0.452\n604\t      - 0.15\n605\t      - 0.64\n606\t  - name: 'Table 2b: Llama 4 Scout Transfer Conditions Summary'\n607\t    columns:\n608\t    - condition\n609\t    - mean_auroc\n610\t    - delta_vs_zs\n611\t    - significant_count\n612\t    rows:\n613\t    - - zero-shot\n614\t      - 0.562\n615\t      - —\n616\t      - —\n617\t    - - mean-shift\n618\t      - 0.562\n619\t      - 0.0\n620\t      - 0/20\n621\t    - - linear_proj_200\n622\t      - 0.598\n623\t      - 0.036\n624\t      - 10/20\n625\t    - - fewshot_25\n626\t      - 0.584\n627\t      - 0.022\n628\t      - 6/20\n629\t    - - fewshot_100\n630\t      - 0.611\n631\t      - 0.049\n632\t      - 12/20\n633\t  figures_description:\n634\t  - 'Figure 2: Llama 4 Scout Pareto scatter, same format as Figure 1a. Cloud 更散乱，\n635\t    global ρ=-0.06 (p=0.31)。ko (+0.35) 和 ja (+0.32) 方向反转于预期。\n636\t\n637\t    '\n638\t  analysis: 'Llama 4 Scout 确认 MoE 架构的 Pareto 缺失。与 Qwen3 合并看：0 个 MoE 架构在 p<0.05 展现\n639\t    Pareto。MVP 中 Llama-3.1-8B 的弱 Pareto 是 dense 架构特有的。两个 MoE 结合表明 expert routing 是\n640\t    Pareto 缺失的结构性原因，而非偶然。\n641\t\n642\t    '\n643\t- name: Gemma 4 31B Dense Pareto Frontier\n644\t  plan_id: plan_008\n645\t  description: 'Gemma 4 31B Dense (60 text layers, BF16 无量化), 16 probed layers (every\n646\t    4th + final), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions. Dense vs MoE 对照。\n647\t\n648\t    '\n649\t  expected_results:\n650\t    en_best_auroc: 0.755\n651\t    en_best_layer: 52\n652\t    en_auroc_range:\n653\t    - 0.618\n654\t    - 0.755\n655\t    en_best_ece_raw: 0.188\n656\t    zs_pass_count_auroc_gt_058: 12\n657\t    zs_pass_rate: 0.6\n658\t    mean_zs_auroc_all_20: 0.585\n659\t    mean_zs_auroc_drop_vs_en_pp: 17.0\n660\t    best_zs_auroc:\n661\t      zh: 0.682\n662\t      es: 0.691\n663\t      fr: 0.672\n664\t      de: 0.665\n665\t      ja: 0.598\n666\t      pt: 0.678\n667\t      it: 0.658\n668\t      ar: 0.618\n669\t      hi: 0.575\n670\t      ru: 0.635\n671\t      ko: 0.602\n672\t      tr: 0.558\n673\t      vi: 0.572\n674\t      th: 0.538\n675\t      sw: 0.525\n676\t      bn: 0.531\n677\t      am: 0.492\n678\t      yo: 0.481\n679\t      te: 0.508\n680\t      my: 0.475\n681\t    global_spearman_rho_depth_vs_transfer: -0.24\n682\t    global_spearman_p: 0.038\n683\t    per_lang_significant_negative_rho_count: 4\n684\t    per_lang_significant_positive_rho_count: 0\n685\t    per_lang_nonmonotonic_count: 5\n686\t    pareto_tradeoff_prevalence: 0.22\n687\t    pareto_depth_transfer_drop_final_layers_pp: 0.8\n688\t    spearman_depth_vs_transfer_rho_positive_langs: 10\n689\t    transfer_conditions_summary:\n690\t      zero_shot:\n691\t        mean_auroc: 0.585\n692\t        std: 0.063\n693\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n694\t      mean_shift:\n695\t        mean_auroc: 0.585\n696\t        std: 0.063\n697\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n698\t      linear_proj_200:\n699\t        mean_auroc: 0.621\n700\t        std: 0.051\n701\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.036\n702\t      fewshot_25:\n703\t        mean_auroc: 0.607\n704\t        std: 0.057\n705\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.022\n706\t      fewshot_100:\n707\t        mean_auroc: 0.634\n708\t        std: 0.045\n709\t        delta_vs_zs: 0.049\n710\t  result_rationale: 'Gemma 4 31B Dense 是唯一有 marginal Pareto 的架构。Dense 架构没有 expert\n711\t    routing， depth→specialization 映射更单调，因此 global rho=-0.24 (p=0.038) 达到 significance。\n712\t    4/20 语言 per-language 显著（zh, fr, hi, sw）——全部是负 rho（deeper layers = worse transfer），\n713\t    符合 specialization 叙述。\n714\t\n715\t    但这反而增加了叙述复杂性：Pareto 是 architecture-dependent 的（dense 有，MoE 没有）， 无法声称是普遍现象。且 final-layer\n716\t    drop 仅 0.8pp——远低于 pilot 的 2-4pp，因为 31B dense model 的最深层已经足够 expressive，EN probe\n717\t    的边际 AUROC 提升很小（L56→L60 仅 +0.4pp）， 相应 transfer 损失也被压缩。\n718\t\n719\t    EN AUROC 0.755 略高于两个 MoE（因无量化损耗 + BF16 保留更多信号精度），三架构均值 (0.741 + 0.718 + 0.755)/3\n720\t    = 0.738，在 worst 范围 [0.72, 0.78] 内。\n721\t\n722\t    ZS pass 12/20 (60%)——三架构最高，因为 Gemma 4 的 multilingual pretraining 可能 更均衡（Apache\n723\t    2.0 开源模型通常 training data 更 curated），且无量化损耗。\n724\t\n725\t    '\n726\t  tables:\n727\t  - name: 'Table 3: Gemma 4 31B Dense Pareto Summary'\n728\t    columns:\n729\t    - metric\n730\t    - value\n731\t    rows:\n732\t    - - en_best_auroc\n733\t      - 0.755\n734\t    - - en_best_layer\n735\t      - L52 (87% depth)\n736\t    - - zs_pass_rate\n737\t      - 60% (12/20)\n738\t    - - global_pareto_rho\n739\t      - -0.24 (p=0.038)\n740\t    - - per_lang_significant_rho\n741\t      - 4/20 (zh, fr, hi, sw)\n742\t    - - final_layer_transfer_drop_pp\n743\t      - 0.8\n744\t    - - control_artifact_rate_LOW\n745\t      - 38%\n746\t    - - no_quantization_confound\n747\t      - BF16 — no quantization artifact\n748\t  - name: 'Table 3b: Dense vs MoE Architecture Comparison'\n749\t    columns:\n750\t    - metric\n751\t    - Qwen3 (MoE)\n752\t    - Llama4 (MoE)\n753\t    - Gemma4 (Dense)\n754\t    rows:\n755\t    - - en_best_auroc\n756\t      - 0.741\n757\t      - 0.718\n758\t      - 0.755\n759\t    - - global_pareto_rho\n760\t      - -0.12 (n.s.)\n761\t      - -0.06 (n.s.)\n762\t      - -0.24 (p=0.038)\n763\t    - - per_lang_sig_count\n764\t      - 1/20\n765\t      - 0/20\n766\t      - 4/20\n767\t    - - non_monotonic_langs\n768\t      - 13/20\n769\t      - 8/20\n770\t      - 5/20\n771\t    - - final_layer_drop_pp\n772\t      - 0.6\n773\t      - 0.3\n774\t      - 0.8\n775\t    - - zs_pass_rate\n776\t      - 55%\n777\t      - 45%\n778\t      - 60%\n779\t  figures_description:\n780\t  - 'Figure 3a: Gemma 4 Pareto scatter vs Qwen3/Llama4 (3-panel). Gemma shows cleaner\n781\t    negative trend but still substantial scatter. MoE panels show diffuse clouds.\n782\t    Visual comparison highlights dense vs MoE structural difference.\n783\t\n784\t    '\n785\t  - 'Figure 3b: Per-language Spearman ρ bar chart across 3 architectures. Gemma bars\n786\t    lean negative but most still n.s. MoE bars scattered around zero.\n787\t\n788\t    '\n789\t  analysis: 'Dense vs MoE 对比是 Gemma 最大的贡献：dense 架构确实有 cleaner depth-transfer 关系， 但\n790\t    effect size 远小于 pilot 预期。三架构综合 pareto_tradeoff_prevalence ≈ 0.12 (12% of lang-arch\n791\t    pairs)，在 worst 范围 [0.05, 0.25] 内。 结论：Pareto 是 architecture-conditional 的，不是 universal\n792\t    finding——这使得 Claim 1 从 \"discovery\" 降级为 \"architecture-dependent observational note\"。\n793\t\n794\t    '\n795\t- name: CaCLR Implementation and Comparative Evaluation\n796\t  plan_id: plan_003\n797\t  description: 'CaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_MMD), β sweep 3 OOM, α sweep, component\n798\t    ablation, CORAL comparison, high-dim MMD (PCA d=50/100), multi-seed (5 seeds),\n799\t    mixed β criterion. vs 4 baselines, 3 models × 20 langs.\n800\t\n801\t    '\n802\t  expected_results:\n803\t    caclr_mean_delta_auroc_vs_zs: -0.008\n804\t    caclr_langs_improved_of_20: 4\n805\t    caclr_best_beta: none — all β inert or harmful\n806\t    beta_sweep:\n807\t      beta_0.001:\n808\t        mean_delta_auroc: -0.002\n809\t        std: 0.016\n810\t      beta_0.01:\n811\t        mean_delta_auroc: -0.005\n812\t        std: 0.019\n813\t      beta_0.1:\n814\t        mean_delta_auroc: -0.009\n815\t        std: 0.023\n816\t      beta_1.0:\n817\t        mean_delta_auroc: -0.016\n818\t        std: 0.028\n819\t    alpha_sweep:\n820\t      alpha_0.01:\n821\t        delta_auroc: -0.001\n822\t        delta_ece: 0.006\n823\t      alpha_0.1:\n824\t        delta_auroc: -0.004\n825\t        delta_ece: 0.002\n826\t      alpha_1.0:\n827\t        delta_auroc: -0.01\n828\t        delta_ece: -0.001\n829\t      alpha_10.0:\n830\t        delta_auroc: -0.025\n831\t        delta_ece: -0.004\n832\t    component_ablation:\n833\t      bce_only:\n834\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.001\n835\t        note: ≈ ZS baseline\n836\t      bce_plus_sbece:\n837\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.005\n838\t        note: SB-ECE hurts discrimination\n839\t      bce_plus_mmd_1d:\n840\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.004\n841\t        note: 1-D MMD inert/harmful\n842\t      bce_plus_mmd_pca50:\n843\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.006\n844\t        note: 50-D MMD also fails\n845\t      bce_plus_mmd_pca100:\n846\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.008\n847\t        note: 100-D MMD worse — curse of dimensionality\n848\t      bce_plus_coral:\n849\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.005\n850\t        note: CORAL fails — second-order alignment insufficient\n851\t      bce_plus_coral_pca50:\n852\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.007\n853\t        note: high-dim CORAL also fails\n854\t      full_caclr:\n855\t        delta_vs_zs: -0.008\n856\t        note: compound degradation\n857\t    multi_seed_std:\n858\t      caclr: 0.003\n859\t      fewshot_25: 0.008\n860\t      fewshot_100: 0.005\n861\t      procrustes: 0.002\n862\t    mixed_beta_criterion_result: 'β selected on zh+sw validation matches English-only\n863\t      selection (β=0.001). No evidence of systematic bias against cross-lingual benefit.\n864\t\n865\t      '\n866\t    five_way_comparison:\n867\t      zero_shot:\n868\t        mean_auroc: 0.574\n869\t        mean_ece: 0.282\n870\t      mean_shift:\n871\t        mean_auroc: 0.574\n872\t        mean_ece: 0.288\n873\t      caclr_best:\n874\t        mean_auroc: 0.566\n875\t        mean_ece: 0.275\n876\t      linear_proj_200:\n877\t        mean_auroc: 0.61\n878\t        mean_ece: 0.245\n879\t      fewshot_25:\n880\t        mean_auroc: 0.596\n881\t        mean_ece: 0.258\n882\t      fewshot_100:\n883\t        mean_auroc: 0.623\n884\t        mean_ece: 0.232\n885\t    implementation_spec:\n886\t      mmd_kernel: Gaussian RBF, bandwidth=median heuristic\n887\t      optimizer: Adam, lr=1e-3, cosine schedule to 1e-5\n888\t      epochs: 50\n889\t      early_stopping: patience=10 on held-out English BCE loss\n890\t      initialization: from standard LR solution\n891\t      batch_size: 256\n892\t      mmd_items: same items as BCE (probe_train 70% split)\n893\t      parallel_set_size_range:\n894\t      - 618\n895\t      - 2852\n896\t  result_rationale: 'CaCLR 失败的根本原因链：\n897\t\n898\t    (1) 1-D MMD 结构性限制：probe logit 是标量，MMD 只能 match 两个 1-D 分布的 marginal。 即使 marginal\n899\t    被 match，EN 和 target 的 conditional distributions P(logit|correct) vs P(logit|incorrect)\n900\t    仍然不同——Zhao et al. (2019) 的理论预测在此得到验证。β 越大，logits 被拉向无区分性的 marginal match，discrimination\n901\t    下降。\n902\t\n903\t    (2) High-dim MMD (PCA d=50/100) 同样失败：curse of dimensionality 使得 Gaussian RBF kernel\n904\t    在 50-100 维空间的 MMD estimate 方差极大，有效样本量不足（probe_train ~2000 samples 对 100 维 MMD\n905\t    来说 severely underpowered）。d=100 比 d=50 更差，证实这一解释。\n906\t\n907\t    (3) CORAL 也失败：second-order alignment（match mean + covariance）比 MMD 更受 conditional\n908\t    distribution mismatch 的影响——对齐 marginal moments 不能修复 correctness signal 的 conditional\n909\t    structure 差异。CORAL 在 domain adaptation 中成功的条件是 covariate shift （P(X) changes,\n910\t    P(Y|X) stable），但 cross-lingual correctness probing 违反这一条件 （P(correct|representation)\n911\t    在不同语言中不同）。\n912\t\n913\t    (4) Component ablation 证实每个额外 loss 都是 net negative：BCE-only retrain ≈ ZS baseline（LR\n914\t    solution 初始化后 Adam 微调不改变 optimum），每加一项都引入额外 noise 而 无 signal。CaCLR 不是超参选择问题而是方法论层面的失败。\n915\t\n916\t    (5) Multi-seed 结果稳定（std=0.003），排除了 single-seed 偶然性。Mixed β criterion 排除了 β selection\n917\t    对 cross-lingual benefit 的系统性偏见。\n918\t\n919\t    综合：distributional matching 路径（MMD + CORAL，low-dim + high-dim）被全面关闭。 Linear projection\n920\t    和 few-shot 显著优于 CaCLR，因为它们直接利用 target-language 结构 信息而非试图间接 match distributions。\n921\t\n922\t    '\n923\t  tables:\n924\t  - name: 'Table 4a: CaCLR β Sweep (3 architectures × 20 langs, EN-optimal layer)'\n925\t    columns:\n926\t    - beta\n927\t    - mean_auroc\n928\t    - delta_vs_zs\n929\t    - pct_improved\n930\t    - pct_harmed\n931\t    rows:\n932\t    - - 0.001\n933\t      - 0.572\n934\t      - -0.002\n935\t      - 30%\n936\t      - 42%\n937\t    - - 0.01\n938\t      - 0.569\n939\t      - -0.005\n940\t      - 25%\n941\t      - 52%\n942\t    - - 0.1\n943\t      - 0.565\n944\t      - -0.009\n945\t      - 18%\n946\t      - 62%\n947\t    - - 1.0\n948\t      - 0.558\n949\t      - -0.016\n950\t      - 12%\n951\t      - 75%\n952\t  - name: 'Table 4b: Distributional Matching Comprehensive Ablation'\n953\t    columns:\n954\t    - method\n955\t    - dimensionality\n956\t    - mean_delta_auroc\n957\t    - note\n958\t    rows:\n959\t    - - MMD (logit)\n960\t      - 1-D\n961\t      - -0.004\n962\t      - marginal match, no conditional alignment\n963\t    - - MMD (PCA-50)\n964\t      - 50-D\n965\t      - -0.006\n966\t      - underpowered MMD in 50-D\n967\t    - - MMD (PCA-100)\n968\t      - 100-D\n969\t      - -0.008\n970\t      - curse of dimensionality\n971\t    - - CORAL (logit)\n972\t      - 1-D\n973\t      - -0.005\n974\t      - second-order alignment insufficient\n975\t    - - CORAL (PCA-50)\n976\t      - 50-D\n977\t      - -0.007\n978\t      - covariance match fails\n979\t    - - Linear projection\n980\t      - full-D Procrustes\n981\t      - 0.036\n982\t      - learns subspace rotation directly\n983\t  - name: 'Table 4c: 5-Way Transfer Comparison (3 arch × 20 langs)'\n984\t    columns:\n985\t    - condition\n986\t    - mean_auroc\n987\t    - mean_ece\n988\t    - delta_auroc_vs_zs\n989\t    - win_rate_vs_zs\n990\t    rows:\n991\t    - - zero-shot\n992\t      - 0.574\n993\t      - 0.282\n994\t      - —\n995\t      - —\n996\t    - - mean-shift\n997\t      - 0.574\n998\t      - 0.288\n999\t      - 0.0\n1000\t      - 0%\n1001\t    - - CaCLR (best)\n1002\t      - 0.566\n1003\t      - 0.275\n1004\t      - -0.008\n1005\t      - 20%\n1006\t    - - linear_proj_200\n1007\t      - 0.61\n1008\t      - 0.245\n1009\t      - 0.036\n1010\t      - 70%\n1011\t    - - fewshot_25\n1012\t      - 0.596\n1013\t      - 0.258\n1014\t      - 0.022\n1015\t      - 52%\n1016\t    - - fewshot_100\n1017\t      - 0.623\n1018\t      - 0.232\n1019\t      - 0.049\n1020\t      - 75%\n1021\t  figures_description:\n1022\t  - 'Figure 4a: β sweep curve showing monotonic decrease in mean AUROC. Shaded 95%\n1023\t    CI all below or crossing zero-shot baseline. Separate lines for MMD-1D, MMD-50D,\n1024\t    MMD-100D, CORAL showing all fail.\n1025\t\n1026\t    '\n1027\t  - 'Figure 4b: Per-language ΔAUROC bars at best β=0.001. Most bars negative. Only\n1028\t    4 HIGH-resource languages show marginal positive Δ within noise margin.\n1029\t\n1030\t    '\n1031\t  - 'Figure 4c: Distributional matching ablation (MMD vs CORAL × dimensionality).\n1032\t    All configurations below zero-shot. Linear projection (rightmost) is the only\n1033\t    positive method. Clean visual separation between distribution-matching (all negative)\n1034\t    and structure-learning (linear projection, positive).\n1035\t\n1036\t    '\n1037\t  analysis: 'CaCLR 的全面 negative result 是 worst tier 的核心贡献之一。关键升级：CORAL + high-dim\n1038\t    MMD 将 scope 从 \"MMD fails\" 扩展为 \"distributional matching path is closed\"。这比仅报告 1-D\n1039\t    MMD 失败有力得多——reviewer 无法反驳说 \"换个 kernel/提高维度就行\"。 Distributional matching ablation\n1040\t    table (Table 4b) 是该 claim 的 anchor evidence。 CKA subspace 解释也不成立（plan_011），所以\n1041\t    geometric rationalization 也失败—— 不仅方法失败，elegant 解释也失败。但完整的 implementation spec\n1042\t    + sweep + ablation 确保 reproducibility，使 negative result 可信。\n1043\t\n1044\t    '\n1045\t- name: Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\n1046\t  plan_id: plan_004\n1047\t  description: 'IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty direction → retrain\n1048\t    correctness probes on residuals → evaluate transfer. 10 representative languages\n1049\t    × 8 representative layers × 3 models. Random-direction control.\n1050\t\n1051\t    '\n1052\t  expected_results:\n1053\t    decomp_transfer_improvement_pp: 0.2\n1054\t    decomp_transfer_improvement_range:\n1055\t    - -0.8\n1056\t    - 1.2\n1057\t    random_direction_control_delta_pp: -0.1\n1058\t    random_direction_control_range:\n1059\t    - -1.0\n1060\t    - 0.8\n1061\t    decomp_vs_random_paired_test_p: 0.38\n1062\t    difficulty_probe_r2: 0.28\n1063\t    decomp_langs_showing_clean_separation: 2\n1064\t    per_tier_results:\n1065\t      HIGH:\n1066\t        mean_delta_pp: 0.3\n1067\t        significant: 0/4\n1068\t        clean_separation: 1\n1069\t      MID:\n1070\t        mean_delta_pp: 0.1\n1071\t        significant: 0/3\n1072\t        clean_separation: 1\n1073\t      LOW:\n1074\t        mean_delta_pp: -0.2\n1075\t        significant: 0/3\n1076\t        clean_separation: 0\n1077\t  result_rationale: 'Decomposition 在 worst tier 无实质效果，两个层面的失败：\n1078\t\n1079\t    (1) Difficulty direction 在 LLM representation 中编码不够 linear/集中——IRT difficulty\n1080\t    probe R²=0.28（低），意味着 linear projection 只捕获了 difficulty variance 的 28%。 剩余 72%\n1081\t    的 difficulty 信息分布在 correctness direction 也占据的子空间中——两者高度 纠缠，projecting out 28%\n1082\t    的 difficulty 同时损坏了部分 correctness signal。\n1083\t\n1084\t    (2) Random-direction control 产生同量级效果（paired test p=0.38），这是 worst tier 的 killer\n1085\t    finding：观察到的微小 delta 主要来自 dimensionality reduction 效应 （投影去除任意方向都会改变 probe 性能 ≈\n1086\t    同量级），而非 difficulty-specific 信号去除。\n1087\t\n1088\t    2/10 语言 \"clean separation\"（zh, ko）可能是 type-I error 在 10 次检验中的自然出现率。 LOW tier 3\n1089\t    语言全部 negative delta——它们的 difficulty 和 capability 信号本身就很弱， 投影去除任何方向只会损失信息。\n1090\t\n1091\t    结论：transfer degradation 不能分解为 difficulty-shared + capability-specific 两个可操作的 component——Claim\n1092\t    2 被否定，decomposition 从 standalone claim 降级。\n1093\t\n1094\t    '\n1095\t  tables:\n1096\t  - name: 'Table 5: Difficulty Decomposition Ablation (3 models mean)'\n1097\t    columns:\n1098\t    - lang\n1099\t    - tier\n1100\t    - original_zs\n1101\t    - after_proj\n1102\t    - delta_pp\n1103\t    - random_ctrl_delta_pp\n1104\t    - paired_p\n1105\t    rows:\n1106\t    - - zh\n1107\t      - HIGH\n1108\t      - 0.666\n1109\t      - 0.67\n1110\t      - 0.4\n1111\t      - 0.1\n1112\t      - 0.45\n1113\t    - - es\n1114\t      - HIGH\n1115\t      - 0.674\n1116\t      - 0.676\n1117\t      - 0.2\n1118\t      - -0.1\n1119\t      - 0.58\n1120\t    - - fr\n1121\t      - HIGH\n1122\t      - 0.657\n1123\t      - 0.66\n1124\t      - 0.3\n1125\t      - 0.2\n1126\t      - 0.82\n1127\t    - - de\n1128\t      - HIGH\n1129\t      - 0.65\n1130\t      - 0.652\n1131\t      - 0.2\n1132\t      - -0.2\n1133\t      - 0.41\n1134\t    - - hi\n1135\t      - MID\n1136\t      - 0.563\n1137\t      - 0.565\n1138\t      - 0.2\n1139\t      - 0.3\n1140\t      - 0.91\n1141\t    - - ru\n1142\t      - MID\n1143\t      - 0.621\n1144\t      - 0.622\n1145\t      - 0.1\n1146\t      - -0.2\n1147\t      - 0.52\n1148\t    - - ko\n1149\t      - MID\n1150\t      - 0.589\n1151\t      - 0.598\n1152\t      - 0.9\n1153\t      - 0.2\n1154\t      - 0.08\n1155\t    - - tr\n1156\t      - MID\n1157\t      - 0.546\n1158\t      - 0.54\n1159\t      - -0.6\n1160\t      - -0.4\n1161\t      - 0.65\n1162\t    - - sw\n1163\t      - LOW\n1164\t      - 0.515\n1165\t      - 0.51\n1166\t      - -0.5\n1167\t      - -0.3\n1168\t      - 0.71\n1169\t    - - bn\n1170\t      - LOW\n1171\t      - 0.521\n1172\t      - 0.519\n1173\t      - -0.2\n1174\t      - 0.0\n1175\t      - 0.68\n1176\t  figures_description:\n1177\t  - 'Figure 5: Paired bar chart of ΔAUROC after difficulty projection (blue) vs random-direction\n1178\t    projection (gray). Error bars = bootstrap 95% CI. All CIs overlap; no language\n1179\t    shows meaningful separation. Vertical dashed line at 0.\n1180\t\n1181\t    '\n1182\t  analysis: 'Decomposition null result 与 random control 不可区分。Claim 2 被否定。 在 worst\n1183\t    tier paper 中这成为另一条被关闭的路径，但不需要大篇幅—— 1 table + 1 figure 在 Section 5.2 用 1 paragraph\n1184\t    报告即可。\n1185\t\n1186\t    '\n1187\t- name: Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\n1188\t  plan_id: plan_005\n1189\t  description: 'Correctness-confidence cosine similarity, 20 languages × 2 architectures\n1190\t    (Qwen3 + Llama4), resource-tier 和 language family 分析.\n1191\t\n1192\t    '\n1193\t  expected_results:\n1194\t    mean_cosine_high: 0.035\n1195\t    mean_cosine_mid: 0.062\n1196\t    mean_cosine_low: 0.108\n1197\t    std_cosine_low: 0.078\n1198\t    cosine_range_all:\n1199\t    - 0.012\n1200\t    - 0.192\n1201\t    architecture_agreement_rate: 0.65\n1202\t    outlier_langs:\n1203\t    - am\n1204\t    - yo\n1205\t    - my\n1206\t  result_rationale: 'Orthogonality 在 HIGH resource 语言成立（cosine < 0.05），复现 Miao & Ungar\n1207\t    (2026)。 但 LOW resource 的 cosine 显著升高且方差大（mean 0.108, std 0.078）——原因不是真正的 非正交结构，而是两个\n1208\t    probe 都更 noisy：correctness probe selectivity 低（plan_013 控制 任务发现），confidence probe\n1209\t    同样缺乏区分性信号，两个 noisy direction 的 cosine 自然 偏离 0。Architecture 一致性仅 65%：7/20 语言两架构给出矛盾信号——可能反映不同\n1210\t    MoE routing 对 confidence 编码方式的影响。\n1211\t\n1212\t    作为已降级的 subsection，这些结果增加复杂性但无 clean takeaway。\n1213\t\n1214\t    '\n1215\t  tables:\n1216\t  - name: 'Table 6: Correctness-Confidence Orthogonality by Resource Tier'\n1217\t    columns:\n1218\t    - tier\n1219\t    - n_langs\n1220\t    - mean_cosine\n1221\t    - std\n1222\t    - min\n1223\t    - max\n1224\t    - arch_agreement\n1225\t    rows:\n1226\t    - - HIGH\n1227\t      - 7\n1228\t      - 0.035\n1229\t      - 0.012\n1230\t      - 0.012\n1231\t      - 0.052\n1232\t      - 6/7\n1233\t    - - MID\n1234\t      - 7\n1235\t      - 0.062\n1236\t      - 0.025\n1237\t      - 0.035\n1238\t      - 0.095\n1239\t      - 5/7\n1240\t    - - LOW\n1241\t      - 6\n1242\t      - 0.108\n1243\t      - 0.078\n1244\t      - 0.042\n1245\t      - 0.192\n1246\t      - 2/6\n1247\t    - - ALL\n1248\t      - 20\n1249\t      - 0.065\n1250\t      - 0.055\n1251\t      - 0.012\n1252\t      - 0.192\n1253\t      - 13/20\n1254\t  figures_description:\n1255\t  - 'Figure S1 (appendix): Box plot of cosine similarity by resource tier, faceted\n1256\t    by architecture. LOW tier shows higher median and wider spread. Dashed line at\n1257\t    cosine=0.10.\n1258\t\n1259\t    '\n1260\t  analysis: 'Orthogonality 作为 subsection 贡献有限。LOW tier 的高 cosine 可能是 probe noise 而非真\n1261\t    non-orthogonality（control task artifact rate 42% in LOW tier）。 简化为 1 paragraph\n1262\t    + 1 table 在 supporting evidence 小节。\n1263\t\n1264\t    '\n1265\t- name: Probe Complexity Comparison\n1266\t  plan_id: plan_006\n1267\t  description: 'Logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP, EN accuracy + cross-lingual transfer\n1268\t    degradation + calibration, 3 models × 20 languages.\n1269\t\n1270\t    '\n1271\t  expected_results:\n1272\t    en_auroc_lr_mean: 0.738\n1273\t    en_auroc_mlp_mean: 0.752\n1274\t    mlp_en_advantage_pp: 1.4\n1275\t    zs_transfer_degradation_lr_pp: 15.8\n1276\t    zs_transfer_degradation_mlp_pp: 19.4\n1277\t    mlp_transfer_disadvantage_pp: 3.6\n1278\t    lr_better_for_transfer_pct: 0.72\n1279\t    ece_lr_mean: 0.238\n1280\t    ece_mlp_mean: 0.252\n1281\t  result_rationale: 'MLP 更高 capacity → EN +1.4pp，但跨语言 transfer degradation 更大（-19.4%\n1282\t    vs -15.8%）， 符合 \"linear probes transfer better\" 假设。在 worst tier 下 effect size 中等\n1283\t    （Cohen''s d ≈ 0.35），72% 语言支持 LR。部分 HIGH resource 语言中 MLP 额外 capacity 弥补了 transfer\n1284\t    loss。结论方向正确但不 dramatic——LR 作为默认 choice 被 confirm， MLP 结果放 appendix。\n1285\t\n1286\t    '\n1287\t  tables:\n1288\t  - name: 'Table S2: Probe Complexity Comparison'\n1289\t    columns:\n1290\t    - metric\n1291\t    - logistic_regression\n1292\t    - mlp_2layer\n1293\t    - delta\n1294\t    - p_value\n1295\t    rows:\n1296\t    - - EN AUROC\n1297\t      - 0.738\n1298\t      - 0.752\n1299\t      - 0.014\n1300\t      - 0.006\n1301\t    - - ZS degradation\n1302\t      - 15.8%\n1303\t      - 19.4%\n1304\t      - +3.6pp\n1305\t      - 0.018\n1306\t    - - ZS AUROC\n1307\t      - 0.621\n1308\t      - 0.608\n1309\t      - -0.013\n1310\t      - 0.032\n1311\t    - - EN ECE\n1312\t      - 0.238\n1313\t      - 0.252\n1314\t      - 0.014\n1315\t      - 0.058\n1316\t    - - LR better for transfer\n1317\t      - 72%\n1318\t      - 28%\n1319\t      - —\n1320\t      - —\n1321\t  figures_description:\n1322\t  - 'Figure S2 (appendix): Layer-wise EN AUROC for LR vs MLP (upper panel) paired\n1323\t    with ZS AUROC (lower panel). MLP advantage grows with EN depth; LR advantage grows\n1324\t    with transfer depth.\n1325\t\n1326\t    '\n1327\t  analysis: '方向符合预期但 effect size 中等。在 worst tier 的 high-artifact 环境下，probe complexity\n1328\t    不是主要问题。保持 LR 默认，appendix 报告 MLP 对比。\n1329\t\n1330\t    '\n1331\t- name: Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\n1332\t  plan_id: plan_007\n1333\t  description: 'Best probes + all transfer conditions on Belebele (20 langs) and MMLU-ProX\n1334\t    (20 langs). Cross-benchmark generalization test.\n1335\t\n1336\t    '\n1337\t  expected_results:\n1338\t    belebele_zs_pass_rate: 0.45\n1339\t    belebele_mean_zs_auroc: 0.545\n1340\t    belebele_vs_globalmmlu_spearman: 0.71\n1341\t    belebele_mean_delta_vs_globalmmlu: -0.029\n1342\t    mmlupx_zs_pass_rate: 0.55\n1343\t    mmlupx_mean_zs_auroc: 0.565\n1344\t    mmlupx_vs_globalmmlu_spearman: 0.79\n1345\t    caclr_belebele_delta: -0.015\n1346\t    caclr_mmlupx_delta: -0.009\n1347\t    linear_proj_belebele_delta: 0.028\n1348\t    linear_proj_mmlupx_delta: 0.033\n1349\t  result_rationale: 'Belebele (reading comprehension) 与 MCQA correctness probing 的\n1350\t    task mismatch 导致更低 pass rate。Correctness probe 在 GlobalMMLU 上学到的 \"correct answer\"\n1351\t    signal 部分依赖于 MCQA-specific format cues（如选项长度、academic domain structure），这些 在 Belebele\n1352\t    的 reading comprehension 中缺失。MMLU-ProX 与 GlobalMMLU 更接近（同为 知识 MCQA），correlation\n1353\t    更高。\n1354\t\n1355\t    CaCLR 在 out-of-distribution data 上更差——distribution mismatch 被放大。 Linear projection\n1356\t    仍正但幅度缩小。\n1357\t\n1358\t    Worst tier 意味着 generalization 弱化了已经微弱的 positive findings， 暗示 correctness probing\n1359\t    可能 MCQA-specific。\n1360\t\n1361\t    '\n1362\t  tables:\n1363\t  - name: 'Table S3: Cross-Benchmark Generalization'\n1364\t    columns:\n1365\t    - benchmark\n1366\t    - zs_pass_rate\n1367\t    - mean_zs_auroc\n1368\t    - caclr_Δ\n1369\t    - linproj_Δ\n1370\t    - corr_vs_globalmmlu\n1371\t    rows:\n1372\t    - - GlobalMMLU\n1373\t      - 57%\n1374\t      - 0.574\n1375\t      - -0.008\n1376\t      - 0.036\n1377\t      - —\n1378\t    - - Belebele\n1379\t      - 45%\n1380\t      - 0.545\n1381\t      - -0.015\n1382\t      - 0.028\n1383\t      - 0.71\n1384\t    - - MMLU-ProX\n1385\t      - 55%\n1386\t      - 0.565\n1387\t      - -0.009\n1388\t      - 0.033\n1389\t      - 0.79\n1390\t  figures_description:\n1391\t  - 'Figure S3 (appendix): Per-language ZS AUROC scatter: GlobalMMLU vs Belebele and\n1392\t    GlobalMMLU vs MMLU-ProX. Moderate positive correlation with visible deviations\n1393\t    for low-resource languages.\n1394\t\n1395\t    '\n1396\t  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark generalization moderate。Belebele 低 performance 暗示 correctness\n1397\t    probing 对 task format 敏感——在 worst tier paper 中增加一层 caveat。 放 appendix 作为 generalization\n1398\t    check。\n1399\t\n1400\t    '\n1401\t- name: Quantization Validation Ablation\n1402\t  plan_id: plan_010\n1403\t  description: '(a) W4A16 vs FP16 for Llama 4 Scout, 5 representative layers, 5% data\n1404\t    subset; (b) INT4 vs FP16 for Qwen3-235B, 5 representative layers, 5% data subset.\n1405\t\n1406\t    '\n1407\t  expected_results:\n1408\t    llama_w4a16_vs_fp16:\n1409\t      mean_delta_auroc: 0.008\n1410\t      max_delta_auroc: 0.016\n1411\t      rank_preservation: 0.92\n1412\t    qwen_int4_vs_fp16:\n1413\t      mean_delta_auroc: 0.011\n1414\t      max_delta_auroc: 0.021\n1415\t      rank_preservation: 0.89\n1416\t    problematic_layers: 2\n1417\t    gemma_note: BF16, no quantization — serves as quantization-free control\n1418\t  result_rationale: 'Quantization artifacts 不灾难性但 non-negligible。深层（80-95% depth）受影响最大，\n1419\t    因为 correctness signal 在这些层最集中，而高频/低方差的 correctness direction 对 quantization noise\n1420\t    更敏感。INT4 (Qwen) 比 W4A16 (Llama) 更aggressive，所以 delta 更大。Rank preservation 88-92%\n1421\t    意味着 per-language ranking 大体保持但不完美。\n1422\t\n1423\t    Worst tier 下这创造一个 caveat：深层 probe 结论 potentially 受量化影响。 Gemma 4 BF16 无量化，提供了 quantization-free\n1424\t    的 architecture 数据点。\n1425\t\n1426\t    '\n1427\t  tables:\n1428\t  - name: 'Table S4: Quantization Validation'\n1429\t    columns:\n1430\t    - model\n1431\t    - quant\n1432\t    - layer_pct\n1433\t    - fp16_auroc\n1434\t    - quant_auroc\n1435\t    - delta\n1436\t    - rank_ok\n1437\t    rows:\n1438\t    - - Llama4\n1439\t      - W4A16\n1440\t      - 20%\n1441\t      - 0.65\n1442\t      - 0.647\n1443\t      - -0.003\n1444\t      - ✓\n1445\t    - - Llama4\n1446\t      - W4A16\n1447\t      - 40%\n1448\t      - 0.675\n1449\t      - 0.668\n1450\t      - -0.007\n1451\t      - ✓\n1452\t    - - Llama4\n1453\t      - W4A16\n1454\t      - 60%\n1455\t      - 0.698\n1456\t      - 0.688\n1457\t      - -0.01\n1458\t      - ✓\n1459\t    - - Llama4\n1460\t      - W4A16\n1461\t      - 80%\n1462\t      - 0.71\n1463\t      - 0.696\n1464\t      - -0.014\n1465\t      - ✗ (2 swaps)\n1466\t    - - Llama4\n1467\t      - W4A16\n1468\t      - 95%\n1469\t      - 0.715\n1470\t      - 0.699\n1471\t      - -0.016\n1472\t      - ✗ (3 swaps)\n1473\t    - - Qwen3\n1474\t      - INT4\n1475\t      - 20%\n1476\t      - 0.628\n1477\t      - 0.623\n1478\t      - -0.005\n1479\t      - ✓\n1480\t    - - Qwen3\n1481\t      - INT4\n1482\t      - 40%\n1483\t      - 0.672\n1484\t      - 0.662\n1485\t      - -0.01\n1486\t      - ✓\n1487\t    - - Qwen3\n1488\t      - INT4\n1489\t      - 60%\n1490\t      - 0.705\n1491\t      - 0.692\n1492\t      - -0.013\n1493\t      - ✗ (1 swap)\n1494\t    - - Qwen3\n1495\t      - INT4\n1496\t      - 80%\n1497\t      - 0.73\n1498\t      - 0.714\n1499\t      - -0.016\n1500\t      - ✗ (3 swaps)\n1501\t    - - Qwen3\n1502\t      - INT4\n1503\t      - 95%\n1504\t      - 0.741\n1505\t      - 0.72\n1506\t      - -0.021\n1507\t      - ✗ (4 swaps)\n1508\t  figures_description:\n1509\t  - 'Figure S4 (appendix): Layer-wise quantization delta for both models. Monotonic\n1510\t    increase in delta with depth. Horizontal dashed line at 1.5pp threshold.\n1511\t\n1512\t    '\n1513\t  analysis: 'Quantization 在深层引入 1-2pp 偏差，不改变主要 negative result 结论 （negative results\n1514\t    不依赖精确数值），但增加 limitations 内容。 Gemma BF16 作为 quantization-free control 点使得 Gemma\n1515\t    的结果最可信。\n1516\t\n1517\t    '\n1518\t- name: CKA Cross-Lingual Representation Similarity Analysis\n1519\t  plan_id: plan_011\n1520\t  description: 'CKA (linear kernel) EN vs target, all probed layers, 20 langs × 3\n1521\t    models. Simpson''s Paradox full-scale validation. Partial correlation controlling\n1522\t    for depth. Same-layer cross-language analysis. Subspace angle analysis.\n1523\t\n1524\t    '\n1525\t  expected_results:\n1526\t    simpson_paradox_confirmed_of_3_arch: 0\n1527\t    partial_correlations:\n1528\t      qwen3:\n1529\t        rho: 0.11\n1530\t        p: 0.28\n1531\t        bootstrap_ci:\n1532\t        - -0.08\n1533\t        - 0.29\n1534\t      llama4:\n1535\t        rho: 0.06\n1536\t        p: 0.45\n1537\t        bootstrap_ci:\n1538\t        - -0.12\n1539\t        - 0.24\n1540\t      gemma4:\n1541\t        rho: 0.16\n1542\t        p: 0.09\n1543\t        bootstrap_ci:\n1544\t        - -0.02\n1545\t        - 0.33\n1546\t    raw_correlations:\n1547\t      qwen3:\n1548\t        rho: -0.32\n1549\t        p: <0.001\n1550\t      llama4:\n1551\t        rho: -0.38\n1552\t        p: <0.001\n1553\t      gemma4:\n1554\t        rho: -0.29\n1555\t        p: <0.001\n1556\t    same_layer_cross_lang_analysis:\n1557\t      qwen3_significant_layers: 2/24\n1558\t      llama4_significant_layers: 0/12\n1559\t      gemma4_significant_layers: 1/16\n1560\t      median_rho: 0.14\n1561\t    subspace_angle:\n1562\t      high_tier_range_deg:\n1563\t      - 15\n1564\t      - 38\n1565\t      mid_tier_range_deg:\n1566\t      - 28\n1567\t      - 52\n1568\t      low_tier_range_deg:\n1569\t      - 42\n1570\t      - 65\n1571\t      consistency_across_layers: low — within-language angle std 8-15° across layers\n1572\t    pilot_replication:\n1573\t      llama_pilot_rho: 0.41\n1574\t      llama_fullscale_rho: 0.06\n1575\t      verdict: pilot artifact confirmed\n1576\t  result_rationale: '这是 worst tier 的 defining falsification。\n1577\t\n1578\t    5 语言 pilot 的 Simpson''s Paradox 被 20 语言全量数据否定：\n1579\t\n1580\t    (1) Llama partial rho 从 +0.41 (p=0.006) 骤降至 +0.06 (p=0.45)。原因：pilot 的 5 语言 恰好\n1581\t    overrepresented CKA-transfer 相关性最强的语言（zh, ar 有高 CKA + 低 degradation）， 排除了关系最弱的语言。15\n1582\t    种新增语言中 MID/LOW tier 的 CKA 模式与 pilot 语言截然不同—— 这些语言的 CKA 虽然也随 depth 下降，但下降斜率和 transfer\n1583\t    degradation 之间没有一致的 within-layer 关系。\n1584\t\n1585\t    (2) Qwen3 rho=+0.11 (p=0.28) 在 pilot 就不显著（+0.18, p=0.274），全量数据只是确认。 Gemma4 rho=+0.16\n1586\t    (p=0.09) 是最接近显著的，但 bootstrap CI 跨零（[-0.02, 0.33]）， 不能依赖。\n1587\t\n1588\t    (3) Same-layer cross-language analysis（n=20 per layer，最强检验）：median rho=0.14， 仅\n1589\t    3/52 层 significant——CKA 在 within-layer 水平几乎无预测力。在同一层中，不同语言 的 CKA 差异巨大但 transfer\n1590\t    AUROC 差异不 track CKA。\n1591\t\n1592\t    (4) Subspace angle analysis 否定 \"correctness direction is a robust language-agnostic\n1593\t    subspace\"：HIGH tier 15-38°（不是近乎平行），LOW tier 42-65°（近乎 orthogonal）。 Angle 在同一语言的不同层之间也有\n1594\t    8-15° 的标准差——correctness direction 不仅跨语言 不一致，在同一语言内也随 depth 漂移。\n1595\t\n1596\t    结论：CKA 不提供超越 depth 的解释力。从 \"geometric analysis\" 降级为 \"suggestive correlation\"——仅保留\n1597\t    CKA heatmap 作为 descriptive visualization。\n1598\t\n1599\t    '\n1600\t  tables:\n1601\t  - name: 'Table 7a: Simpson''s Paradox Full-Scale Validation'\n1602\t    columns:\n1603\t    - model\n1604\t    - raw_rho\n1605\t    - raw_p\n1606\t    - partial_rho\n1607\t    - partial_p\n1608\t    - pilot_rho\n1609\t    - pilot_p\n1610\t    - verdict\n1611\t    rows:\n1612\t    - - Qwen3-235B\n1613\t      - -0.32\n1614\t      - <0.001\n1615\t      - 0.11\n1616\t      - 0.28\n1617\t      - +0.18 (n.s.)\n1618\t      - 0.274\n1619\t      - n.s. confirmed\n1620\t    - - Llama4-Scout\n1621\t      - -0.38\n1622\t      - <0.001\n1623\t      - 0.06\n1624\t      - 0.45\n1625\t      - +0.41 (sig.)\n1626\t      - 0.006\n1627\t      - pilot artifact\n1628\t    - - Gemma4-31B\n1629\t      - -0.29\n1630\t      - <0.001\n1631\t      - 0.16\n1632\t      - 0.09\n1633\t      - N/A\n1634\t      - N/A\n1635\t      - marginal, CI spans 0\n1636\t  - name: 'Table 7b: Same-Layer Cross-Language CKA-Transfer Correlation'\n1637\t    columns:\n1638\t    - model\n1639\t    - total_layers\n1640\t    - significant_layers\n1641\t    - median_rho\n1642\t    - best_layer_rho\n1643\t    - best_p\n1644\t    rows:\n1645\t    - - Qwen3\n1646\t      - 24\n1647\t      - 2/24\n1648\t      - 0.15\n1649\t      - 0.4\n1650\t      - 0.078\n1651\t    - - Llama4\n1652\t      - 12\n1653\t      - 0/12\n1654\t      - 0.08\n1655\t      - 0.28\n1656\t      - 0.23\n1657\t    - - Gemma4\n1658\t      - 16\n1659\t      - 1/16\n1660\t      - 0.18\n1661\t      - 0.44\n1662\t      - 0.052\n1663\t  - name: 'Table 7c: Subspace Angle (Correctness Direction, EN vs Target, at ~60%\n1664\t      depth)'\n1665\t    columns:\n1666\t    - lang\n1667\t    - tier\n1668\t    - qwen3_angle\n1669\t    - llama4_angle\n1670\t    - gemma4_angle\n1671\t    rows:\n1672\t    - - zh\n1673\t      - HIGH\n1674\t      - 18°\n1675\t      - 24°\n1676\t      - 16°\n1677\t    - - es\n1678\t      - HIGH\n1679\t      - 15°\n1680\t      - 20°\n1681\t      - 14°\n1682\t    - - ja\n1683\t      - HIGH\n1684\t      - 35°\n1685\t      - 42°\n1686\t      - 32°\n1687\t    - - ar\n1688\t      - MID\n1689\t      - 32°\n1690\t      - 40°\n1691\t      - 30°\n1692\t    - - hi\n1693\t      - MID\n1694\t      - 38°\n1695\t      - 46°\n1696\t      - 35°\n1697\t    - - ko\n1698\t      - MID\n1699\t      - 28°\n1700\t      - 36°\n1701\t      - 26°\n1702\t    - - tr\n1703\t      - MID\n1704\t      - 45°\n1705\t      - 52°\n1706\t      - 42°\n1707\t    - - sw\n1708\t      - LOW\n1709\t      - 52°\n1710\t      - 58°\n1711\t      - 48°\n1712\t    - - bn\n1713\t      - LOW\n1714\t      - 48°\n1715\t      - 55°\n1716\t      - 45°\n1717\t    - - am\n1718\t      - LOW\n1719\t      - 62°\n1720\t      - 65°\n1721\t      - 58°\n1722\t  figures_description:\n1723\t  - 'Figure 6a: CKA heatmap (language × layer) for 3 models. Shows CKA decline with\n1724\t    depth but no clear correspondence to transfer patterns. Color-coded annotations\n1725\t    marking same-layer significant correlations (rare).\n1726\t\n1727\t    '\n1728\t  - 'Figure 6b: Partial residual scatter (CKA residualized on depth vs transfer AUROC\n1729\t    residualized on depth) for 3 models. Diffuse clouds with no visible trend.\n1730\t\n1731\t    '\n1732\t  - 'Figure 6c: Subspace angle violin plot by resource tier across 3 architectures.\n1733\t    Clear tier gradient but HIGH tier also 15-38° range, undermining \"language-agnostic\n1734\t    subspace\" claim. LOW tier near orthogonal.\n1735\t\n1736\t    '\n1737\t  analysis: 'CKA 的全面失败从 pilot 的 Simpson''s Paradox 标杆发现降级为 \"depth confound 在 raw correlation\n1738\t    中占主导，controlling 后无 signal\"。Subspace angle 否定了论文的 前提假设：\"correctness direction\n1739\t    是 robust language-agnostic subspace\" 不成立。 CKA 框架从解释性分析降级为描述性可视化——保留 heatmap 但不承载因果叙述。\n1740\t    3 架构 0/3 Simpson''s Paradox confirmed，在 worst 范围 [0, 1] 内。\n1741\t\n1742\t    '\n1743\t- name: Linear Projection Sensitivity Analysis\n1744\t  plan_id: plan_012\n1745\t  description: 'Procrustes alignment with 10/20/50/100/200 parallel pairs. 3 models\n1746\t    × 5 representative layers × 20 languages.\n1747\t\n1748\t    '\n1749\t  expected_results:\n1750\t    linear_proj_delta_over_zs_low_resource_pp: 2.8\n1751\t    linear_proj_saturation_pairs_mean: 135\n1752\t    saturation_by_tier:\n1753\t      HIGH:\n1754\t        pairs_95pct: 62\n1755\t        range:\n1756\t        - 38\n1757\t        - 92\n1758\t      MID:\n1759\t        pairs_95pct: 118\n1760\t        range:\n1761\t        - 72\n1762\t        - 158\n1763\t      LOW:\n1764\t        pairs_95pct: 175\n1765\t        range:\n1766\t        - 140\n1767\t        - 198\n1768\t    sample_efficiency_curve:\n1769\t      10_pairs:\n1770\t        mean_auroc: 0.552\n1771\t        pct_of_200: 66%\n1772\t      20_pairs:\n1773\t        mean_auroc: 0.571\n1774\t        pct_of_200: 78%\n1775\t      50_pairs:\n1776\t        mean_auroc: 0.592\n1777\t        pct_of_200: 89%\n1778\t      100_pairs:\n1779\t        mean_auroc: 0.605\n1780\t        pct_of_200: 96%\n1781\t      200_pairs:\n1782\t        mean_auroc: 0.61\n1783\t        pct_of_200: 100%\n1784\t    procrustes_reversal:\n1785\t      helps_below_zs: < 0.53 (mostly helps)\n1786\t      hurts_above_zs: '> 0.62 (mostly hurts)'\n1787\t      inconsistent_zone:\n1788\t      - 0.53\n1789\t      - 0.62\n1790\t      note: threshold varies ±0.08 across languages — no single reliable cutoff\n1791\t  result_rationale: 'Worst tier 下 linear projection 需 100-135 pairs 达到 95% performance（非\n1792\t    50）：\n1793\t\n1794\t    (1) Subspace angle 在 worst tier 更大更不一致（plan_011），Procrustes 需更多数据 稳定 rotation\n1795\t    matrix 估计——50 pairs 在高维空间 rank-deficient。\n1796\t\n1797\t    (2) LOW resource 语言的 parallel pairs 翻译质量低 → activation noise → 需更多 pairs average\n1798\t    out noise。HIGH tier 62 pairs（翻译精确，subspace angle 小）vs LOW tier 175 pairs（翻译 noisy，subspace\n1799\t    angle 大）。\n1800\t\n1801\t    (3) Effect reversal threshold language-specific：inconsistent zone [0.53, 0.62]\n1802\t    意味着同一 ZS AUROC 值下不同语言可能被帮助或伤害。例如 ja (HIGH, ZS=0.588) 被 帮助但 ko (MID, ZS=0.589)\n1803\t    被伤害——差异来自 subspace angle 和翻译质量的交互作用。 无法给出单一可操作阈值——practitioner recommendation\n1804\t    弱化为 \"ZS < 0.50 大概率有益， > 0.65 大概率有害，中间区间需 held-out validation\"。\n1805\t\n1806\t    低资源语言 delta +2.8pp（worst 范围 [1, 4] 内），仍是唯一可行的 label-free 方案。\n1807\t\n1808\t    '\n1809\t  tables:\n1810\t  - name: 'Table 8a: Linear Projection Sample Efficiency (3 arch × 20 langs)'\n1811\t    columns:\n1812\t    - n_pairs\n1813\t    - mean_auroc\n1814\t    - pct_of_200\n1815\t    - std\n1816\t    - significant_pct\n1817\t    rows:\n1818\t    - - 10\n1819\t      - 0.552\n1820\t      - 66%\n1821\t      - 0.062\n1822\t      - 22%\n1823\t    - - 20\n1824\t      - 0.571\n1825\t      - 78%\n1826\t      - 0.055\n1827\t      - 38%\n1828\t    - - 50\n1829\t      - 0.592\n1830\t      - 89%\n1831\t      - 0.049\n1832\t      - 52%\n1833\t    - - 100\n1834\t      - 0.605\n1835\t      - 96%\n1836\t      - 0.044\n1837\t      - 65%\n1838\t    - - 200\n1839\t      - 0.61\n1840\t      - 100%\n1841\t      - 0.042\n1842\t      - 70%\n1843\t  - name: 'Table 8b: Pairs to 95% by Resource Tier'\n1844\t    columns:\n1845\t    - tier\n1846\t    - mean\n1847\t    - min\n1848\t    - max\n1849\t    - std\n1850\t    rows:\n1851\t    - - HIGH\n1852\t      - 62\n1853\t      - 38\n1854\t      - 92\n1855\t      - 20\n1856\t    - - MID\n1857\t      - 118\n1858\t      - 72\n1859\t      - 158\n1860\t      - 32\n1861\t    - - LOW\n1862\t      - 175\n1863\t      - 140\n1864\t      - 198\n1865\t      - 25\n1866\t  - name: 'Table 8c: Procrustes Effect Direction (200 pairs, selected languages)'\n1867\t    columns:\n1868\t    - lang\n1869\t    - tier\n1870\t    - zs_auroc\n1871\t    - linproj_auroc\n1872\t    - delta\n1873\t    - effect\n1874\t    rows:\n1875\t    - - am\n1876\t      - LOW\n1877\t      - 0.483\n1878\t      - 0.508\n1879\t      - 0.025\n1880\t      - helps\n1881\t    - - yo\n1882\t      - LOW\n1883\t      - 0.468\n1884\t      - 0.494\n1885\t      - 0.026\n1886\t      - helps\n1887\t    - - sw\n1888\t      - LOW\n1889\t      - 0.511\n1890\t      - 0.528\n1891\t      - 0.017\n1892\t      - helps\n1893\t    - - tr\n1894\t      - MID\n1895\t      - 0.544\n1896\t      - 0.56\n1897\t      - 0.016\n1898\t      - helps\n1899\t    - - hi\n1900\t      - MID\n1901\t      - 0.56\n1902\t      - 0.568\n1903\t      - 0.008\n1904\t      - marginal\n1905\t    - - vi\n1906\t      - MID\n1907\t      - 0.563\n1908\t      - 0.562\n1909\t      - -0.001\n1910\t      - neutral\n1911\t    - - ko\n1912\t      - MID\n1913\t      - 0.589\n1914\t      - 0.582\n1915\t      - -0.007\n1916\t      - hurts\n1917\t    - - ar\n1918\t      - MID\n1919\t      - 0.606\n1920\t      - 0.598\n1921\t      - -0.008\n1922\t      - hurts\n1923\t    - - ru\n1924\t      - MID\n1925\t      - 0.622\n1926\t      - 0.61\n1927\t      - -0.012\n1928\t      - hurts\n1929\t    - - es\n1930\t      - HIGH\n1931\t      - 0.674\n1932\t      - 0.654\n1933\t      - -0.02\n1934\t      - hurts\n1935\t    - - ja\n1936\t      - HIGH\n1937\t      - 0.588\n1938\t      - 0.596\n1939\t      - 0.008\n1940\t      - helps (despite HIGH)\n1941\t  figures_description:\n1942\t  - 'Figure 7a: Saturation curves faceted by resource tier, 95% threshold marked.\n1943\t    Per-language thin lines show within-tier variance. HIGH saturates early, LOW late.\n1944\t\n1945\t    '\n1946\t  - 'Figure 7b: ZS AUROC (x) vs ΔAUROC (y) scatter. Rough negative trend but wide\n1947\t    scatter band. Shaded inconsistent zone [0.53, 0.62] where both ± deltas occur.\n1948\t\n1949\t    '\n1950\t  analysis: 'Linear projection 是唯一可行 label-free 方案但实用性弱化：需 100+ pairs（非 50）， effect\n1951\t    reversal threshold inconsistent。Paper 给出条件性 recommendation： \"ZS < 0.50 大概率有益,\n1952\t    > 0.65 大概率有害, 中间需 validation\"—— 比预期的 clean threshold 弱得多，但对 practitioners 仍有指导价值。\n1953\t\n1954\t    '\n1955\t- name: Probing Control Tasks — Cross-Lingual Extension\n1956\t  plan_id: plan_013\n1957\t  description: 'Hewitt & Liang control tasks extended to 20 languages × all probed\n1958\t    layers × 3 models. Selectivity analysis. Multiple selectivity thresholds (0.03,\n1959\t    0.05, 0.10). (builds on completed plan_013 EN-only results)\n1960\t\n1961\t    '\n1962\t  expected_results:\n1963\t    cross_lingual_artifact_rate_pct: 35\n1964\t    artifact_by_tier:\n1965\t      HIGH:\n1966\t        rate: 15%\n1967\t        selectivity_mean: 0.195\n1968\t      MID:\n1969\t        rate: 31%\n1970\t        selectivity_mean: 0.138\n1971\t      LOW:\n1972\t        rate: 42%\n1973\t        selectivity_mean: 0.082\n1974\t    control_task_selectivity_deep_layers: 0.16\n1975\t    selectivity_vs_zs_auroc_rho: 0.65\n1976\t    threshold_sensitivity:\n1977\t      threshold_003:\n1978\t        artifact_rate: 42%\n1979\t      threshold_005:\n1980\t        artifact_rate: 35%\n1981\t      threshold_010:\n1982\t        artifact_rate: 24%\n1983\t    worst_combos:\n1984\t    - 'am: selectivity 0.004 at EN-opt layer'\n1985\t    - 'yo: selectivity 0.005 at EN-opt layer'\n1986\t    - 'my: selectivity 0.006 at EN-opt layer'\n1987\t    - 'sw: selectivity 0.008 at EN-opt layer'\n1988\t    mid_resource_surprise:\n1989\t      tr:\n1990\t        selectivity_at_enopt: 0.031\n1991\t      th:\n1992\t        selectivity_at_enopt: 0.028\n1993\t      vi:\n1994\t        selectivity_at_enopt: 0.042\n1995\t  result_rationale: 'Cross-lingual artifact rate 35% (overall) 是 worst tier 最强贡献。\n1996\t\n1997\t    LOW tier 42% artifact rate 的原因：am, yo, my, te 等语言在 LLM pretraining 中 极度不足（估计 <\n1998\t    0.1% token share），这些语言的 representation 缺乏区分性结构—— probe 学到的主要是 capacity artifacts（随机\n1999\t    label 也能达到类似 AUROC）。 Selectivity = real_AUROC - permuted_AUROC 对这些语言仅 0.004-0.008，\n2000\t    几乎等于 zero information content。\n2001\t\n2002\t    MID tier 31% artifact rate 是 worst tier 的 signature finding：不仅低资源有问题—— tr (0.031),\n2003\t    th (0.028), vi (0.042) 等中资源语言在 shallow/mid layers 也有大量 artifacts。原因：这些语言虽然 pretraining\n2004\t    充足，但 correctness-specific signal （区分 \"模型答对/答错\"）在 representation 中的编码弱于语言 identity\n2005\t    signal， probe 部分地拟合了 language-specific capacity pattern 而非 correctness。\n2006\t\n2007\t    HIGH tier 15% artifact rate 主要出现在 shallow layers（0-30% depth）， 与 plan_013 completed\n2008\t    results 一致（L0-L16 selectivity < 0.12）。\n2009\t\n2010\t    Selectivity 与 ZS AUROC 的 rho=0.65 是最尖锐的发现：暗示 cross-lingual probing 文献中许多 \"positive\n2011\t    transfer\" 结果可能是 artifacts——高 ZS AUROC 可能部分反映 capacity artifacts 而非 genuine correctness\n2012\t    signal transfer。\n2013\t\n2014\t    首次在 cross-lingual transfer 场景系统性应用 Hewitt & Liang selectivity—— 发现 artifact 问题远比\n2015\t    monolingual probing 严重。Field-level implication。\n2016\t\n2017\t    '\n2018\t  tables:\n2019\t  - name: 'Table 9a: Cross-Lingual Artifact Rate by Resource Tier (3 models)'\n2020\t    columns:\n2021\t    - tier\n2022\t    - n_langs\n2023\t    - artifact_rate_thresh_005\n2024\t    - selectivity_mean\n2025\t    - selectivity_std\n2026\t    rows:\n2027\t    - - HIGH\n2028\t      - 7\n2029\t      - 15%\n2030\t      - 0.195\n2031\t      - 0.042\n2032\t    - - MID\n2033\t      - 7\n2034\t      - 31%\n2035\t      - 0.138\n2036\t      - 0.038\n2037\t    - - LOW\n2038\t      - 6\n2039\t      - 42%\n2040\t      - 0.082\n2041\t      - 0.035\n2042\t    - - ALL\n2043\t      - 20\n2044\t      - 35%\n2045\t      - 0.142\n2046\t      - 0.058\n2047\t  - name: 'Table 9b: Per-Language Selectivity at EN-Optimal Layer (Qwen3)'\n2048\t    columns:\n2049\t    - lang\n2050\t    - tier\n2051\t    - real_auroc\n2052\t    - permuted_auroc\n2053\t    - selectivity\n2054\t    - flag\n2055\t    rows:\n2056\t    - - en\n2057\t      - —\n2058\t      - 0.741\n2059\t      - 0.488\n2060\t      - 0.253\n2061\t      - ''\n2062\t    - - zh\n2063\t      - HIGH\n2064\t      - 0.668\n2065\t      - 0.495\n2066\t      - 0.173\n2067\t      - ''\n2068\t    - - es\n2069\t      - HIGH\n2070\t      - 0.675\n2071\t      - 0.492\n2072\t      - 0.183\n2073\t      - ''\n2074\t    - - fr\n2075\t      - HIGH\n2076\t      - 0.658\n2077\t      - 0.49\n2078\t      - 0.168\n2079\t      - ''\n2080\t    - - de\n2081\t      - HIGH\n2082\t      - 0.649\n2083\t      - 0.486\n2084\t      - 0.163\n2085\t      - ''\n2086\t    - - ja\n2087\t      - HIGH\n2088\t      - 0.588\n2089\t      - 0.501\n2090\t      - 0.087\n2091\t      - ''\n2092\t    - - pt\n2093\t      - HIGH\n2094\t      - 0.662\n2095\t      - 0.489\n2096\t      - 0.173\n2097\t      - ''\n2098\t    - - it\n2099\t      - HIGH\n2100\t      - 0.645\n2101\t      - 0.492\n2102\t      - 0.153\n2103\t      - ''\n2104\t    - - ar\n2105\t      - MID\n2106\t      - 0.608\n2107\t      - 0.496\n2108\t      - 0.112\n2109\t      - ''\n2110\t    - - hi\n2111\t      - MID\n2112\t      - 0.567\n2113\t      - 0.503\n2114\t      - 0.064\n2115\t      - ⚠\n2116\t    - - ru\n2117\t      - MID\n2118\t      - 0.621\n2119\t      - 0.493\n2120\t      - 0.128\n2121\t      - ''\n2122\t    - - ko\n2123\t      - MID\n2124\t      - 0.591\n2125\t      - 0.499\n2126\t      - 0.092\n2127\t      - ''\n2128\t    - - tr\n2129\t      - MID\n2130\t      - 0.548\n2131\t      - 0.517\n2132\t      - 0.031\n2133\t      - ⚠\n2134\t    - - vi\n2135\t      - MID\n2136\t      - 0.562\n2137\t      - 0.52\n2138\t      - 0.042\n2139\t      - ⚠\n2140\t    - - th\n2141\t      - MID\n2142\t      - 0.528\n2143\t      - 0.5\n2144\t      - 0.028\n2145\t      - ⚠\n2146\t    - - sw\n2147\t      - LOW\n2148\t      - 0.518\n2149\t      - 0.51\n2150\t      - 0.008\n2151\t      - ⚠⚠\n2152\t    - - bn\n2153\t      - LOW\n2154\t      - 0.524\n2155\t      - 0.505\n2156\t      - 0.019\n2157\t      - ⚠⚠\n2158\t    - - am\n2159\t      - LOW\n2160\t      - 0.486\n2161\t      - 0.482\n2162\t      - 0.004\n2163\t      - ⚠⚠\n2164\t    - - yo\n2165\t      - LOW\n2166\t      - 0.475\n2167\t      - 0.47\n2168\t      - 0.005\n2169\t      - ⚠⚠\n2170\t    - - te\n2171\t      - LOW\n2172\t      - 0.502\n2173\t      - 0.492\n2174\t      - 0.01\n2175\t      - ⚠⚠\n2176\t    - - my\n2177\t      - LOW\n2178\t      - 0.468\n2179\t      - 0.462\n2180\t      - 0.006\n2181\t      - ⚠⚠\n2182\t  - name: 'Table 9c: Selectivity Threshold Sensitivity'\n2183\t    columns:\n2184\t    - threshold\n2185\t    - overall_artifact_rate\n2186\t    - LOW_rate\n2187\t    - MID_rate\n2188\t    - HIGH_rate\n2189\t    rows:\n2190\t    - - 0.03\n2191\t      - 42%\n2192\t      - 52%\n2193\t      - 40%\n2194\t      - 22%\n2195\t    - - 0.05\n2196\t      - 35%\n2197\t      - 42%\n2198\t      - 31%\n2199\t      - 15%\n2200\t    - - 0.1\n2201\t      - 24%\n2202\t      - 35%\n2203\t      - 22%\n2204\t      - 8%\n2205\t  figures_description:\n2206\t  - 'Figure 8a: Selectivity heatmap (language × layer) for Qwen3-235B. Color scale:\n2207\t    red (<0.05) → yellow (0.05-0.10) → green (>0.20). Large red region in LOW × shallow\n2208\t    layers. MID-resource red patches at moderate depths are the surprise finding.\n2209\t\n2210\t    '\n2211\t  - 'Figure 8b: Selectivity vs ZS AUROC scatter across all language-layer-model combinations.\n2212\t    Strong positive correlation (ρ=0.65). Annotation: \"Many ''successful'' transfer\n2213\t    results fall in the low-selectivity region.\"\n2214\t\n2215\t    '\n2216\t  - 'Figure 8c: Artifact rate by resource tier with bootstrap 95% CI. MID tier CI\n2217\t    overlaps substantially with LOW tier — the problem is not confined to low-resource\n2218\t    languages.\n2219\t\n2220\t    '\n2221\t  analysis: 'Control task finding 是 worst tier paper 的 anchor contribution。>35% artifact\n2222\t    rate 波及中资源语言是 field-level 发现：所有跨语言 probing 研究——包括只看中/高资源的—— 都需要 selectivity 检验。Selectivity-AUROC\n2223\t    correlation (ρ=0.65) 暗示文献中许多 positive results 可能是 artifacts。首次系统性应用 Hewitt & Liang\n2224\t    到 cross-lingual 场景——这个贡献独立于本文其他所有 claims，即使其他全部失败仍足以支撑 EACL findings paper。\n2225\t\n2226\t    '\n2227\t- name: Extended Language Coverage (50+ Languages)\n2228\t  plan_id: plan_009\n2229\t  description: '从 20 扩展到 50+ 语言 (camera-ready extension)。Leverages GlobalMMLU/Belebele\n2230\t    full language sets。P2 priority。\n2231\t\n2232\t    '\n2233\t  expected_results:\n2234\t    total_languages: 52\n2235\t    zs_pass_rate_52lang: 0.5\n2236\t    artifact_rate_low_expanded: 0.45\n2237\t    artifact_rate_mid_expanded: 0.34\n2238\t    new_significant_pareto_langs: 2\n2239\t    linear_proj_saturation_mean_expanded: 155\n2240\t  result_rationale: '扩展到 52 语言后新增大部分是 MID/LOW resource，ZS pass rate 从 57% → 50% 因为新语言\n2241\t    skew lower resource。Control artifact rate 在扩展 LOW tier 升至 45% 因为更多极低资源语言纳入。新增语言不改变核心\n2242\t    negative results，主要增加 statistical power 和 coverage credibility。Linear projection\n2243\t    saturation mean 升至 155 因为 更多 hard languages。\n2244\t\n2245\t    扩展语言数的主要价值：(1) control task finding 的 scope 更大——\"近半数低资源跨语言 probing 结果是 artifacts\"\n2246\t    在 50+ 语言规模下更有说服力；(2) EACL reviewer 可能要求 更多语言的 coverage；(3) 无量化 Gemma 在 52 语言上的数据最可信。\n2247\t\n2248\t    '\n2249\t  tables:\n2250\t  - name: 'Table S5: 52-Language vs 20-Language Summary'\n2251\t    columns:\n2252\t    - metric\n2253\t    - 20_lang\n2254\t    - 52_lang\n2255\t    - delta\n2256\t    rows:\n2257\t    - - zs_pass_rate\n2258\t      - 57%\n2259\t      - 50%\n2260\t      - -7pp\n2261\t    - - artifact_rate_LOW\n2262\t      - 42%\n2263\t      - 45%\n2264\t      - +3pp\n2265\t    - - artifact_rate_MID\n2266\t      - 31%\n2267\t      - 34%\n2268\t      - +3pp\n2269\t    - - linear_proj_mean_pairs\n2270\t      - 135\n2271\t      - 155\n2272\t      - '+20'\n2273\t    - - max_partial_rho\n2274\t      - 0.16\n2275\t      - 0.14\n2276\t      - '-0.02'\n2277\t  figures_description:\n2278\t  - 'Figure S5 (camera-ready): World map of ZS AUROC at EN-optimal layer with artifact\n2279\t    flags. Sub-Saharan Africa and Southeast Asia dominated by artifact flags. Latin-script\n2280\t    European cluster relatively clean.\n2281\t\n2282\t    '\n2283\t  analysis: '52 语言扩展服务于 coverage 和 robustness。核心结论不变但 control task finding 更 impactful，linear\n2284\t    projection guidance 更 granular（更多语言的 tier classification）。\n2285\t\n2286\t    '\n2287\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4ed7333-11c6-492f-a8d4-e66619498d15","uuid":"1887214f-ffda-49d0-9d96-1893ccfc83bd","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:57:06.440Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122458/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '7-8B pilot 的核心模式不推广到全量模型。两个 MoE 架构（Qwen3-235B, Llama 4 Scout）完全没有清晰的\n  Pareto frontier——MoE expert routing 打破了 dense model 中 depth→specialization 的单调映射，\n  depth-transfer 关系在绝大多数语言为 non-monotonic 或 flat。唯一的 dense 架构（Gemma 4 31B）展现出 marginal\n  Pareto（global rho=-0.24, p=0.038），但仅 4/20 语言 per-language 显著，且 final-layer transfer\n  drop 微不足道（0.8pp），远不及 pilot 的 2-4pp。三架构平均 EN AUROC 0.74，处于 worst 范围中段。\n\n  Simpson''s Paradox 在 20 语言全量验证中全面崩塌：3 架构的 CKA partial correlation controlling for\n  depth 均不显著（max rho=+0.16, min p=0.09），Llama pilot 的 rho=+0.41 被确认为 5 语言 small-sample\n  artifact。CKA 提供不了超越 depth 的解释力。Subspace angle analysis 否定了 \"correctness direction\n  is a robust language-agnostic subspace\"——HIGH tier 语言 angle 15-38°，LOW tier 45-65°。\n\n  CaCLR 全面失败：β sweep 3 OOM 证实 consistency loss inert 或 harmful；CORAL 和 high-dim MMD\n  (PCA d=50/100) 同样失败，将 negative result 从 \"MMD-specific\" 扩展为 \"distributional matching\n  路径全面 关闭\"。Component ablation 每加一项 loss 都 net negative。\n\n  Decomposition 无实质效果，random-direction control 产生同量级 delta（paired test p=0.38）， difficulty\n  和 capability 不可分。\n\n  Control task analysis 是最强贡献：cross-lingual artifact rate 达 35%（LOW 42%，MID 31%，HIGH\n  15%）， 首次在跨语言 probing 场景系统性应用 selectivity 检验。Selectivity 与 ZS AUROC 强相关（rho=0.65），\n  暗示文献中许多 positive transfer 结果可能是 capacity artifacts。\n\n  Linear projection 作为唯一可行方案但需 100+ pairs（非 50），且效果反转阈值 language-specific， 无法给出单一可操作的\n  cutoff。\n\n  重构为 EACL negative results + methodology paper：(1) control task 方法论警告（field-level\n  贡献）， (2) mean-shift 不可能性证明（理论贡献），(3) distributional matching 路径全面关闭（CaCLR + CORAL\n  + high-dim MMD 系统性 negative result），(4) linear projection 条件性实用指导（descriptive empirical\n  贡献）。Drop Claim 2（decomposition）和 Claim 3（CaCLR method）作为 standalone claims。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Qwen3-235B Full Pareto Frontier\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: 'Qwen3-235B-A22B (94 layers, MoE, INT4), 24 probed layers (every 4th),\n    20 typologically diverse languages, EN correctness probes (LR + MLP), 5 transfer\n    conditions (zero-shot, mean-shift, linear projection 200 pairs, few-shot 25/100,\n    CaCLR).\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_best_auroc: 0.741\n    en_best_layer: 72\n    en_auroc_range:\n    - 0.601\n    - 0.741\n    en_best_ece_raw: 0.198\n    zs_pass_count_auroc_gt_058: 11\n    zs_pass_rate: 0.55\n    zs_fail_count: 9\n    mean_zs_auroc_all_20: 0.576\n    mean_zs_auroc_drop_vs_en_pp: 16.5\n    best_zs_auroc:\n      zh: 0.668\n      es: 0.675\n      fr: 0.658\n      de: 0.649\n      ja: 0.588\n      pt: 0.662\n      it: 0.645\n      ar: 0.608\n      hi: 0.567\n      ru: 0.621\n      ko: 0.591\n      tr: 0.548\n      vi: 0.562\n      th: 0.528\n      sw: 0.518\n      bn: 0.524\n      am: 0.486\n      yo: 0.475\n      te: 0.502\n      my: 0.468\n    best_zs_layer:\n      zh: 60\n      es: 56\n      fr: 60\n      de: 52\n      ja: 48\n      pt: 56\n      it: 56\n      ar: 52\n      hi: 44\n      ru: 56\n      ko: 48\n      tr: 40\n      vi: 44\n      th: 36\n      sw: 36\n      bn: 40\n      am: 32\n      yo: 28\n      te: 36\n      my: 32\n    global_spearman_rho_depth_vs_transfer: -0.12\n    global_spearman_p: 0.078\n    per_lang_spearman:\n      zh:\n        rho: -0.31\n        p: 0.14\n      es:\n        rho: -0.25\n        p: 0.24\n      fr:\n        rho: -0.28\n        p: 0.18\n      de:\n        rho: -0.19\n        p: 0.38\n      ja:\n        rho: 0.18\n        p: 0.4\n      pt:\n        rho: -0.22\n        p: 0.3\n      it:\n        rho: -0.16\n        p: 0.46\n      ar:\n        rho: 0.05\n        p: 0.82\n      hi:\n        rho: -0.41\n        p: 0.046\n      ru:\n        rho: -0.14\n        p: 0.52\n      ko:\n        rho: 0.25\n        p: 0.24\n      tr:\n        rho: -0.08\n        p: 0.71\n      vi:\n        rho: 0.09\n        p: 0.68\n      th:\n        rho: -0.11\n        p: 0.61\n      sw:\n        rho: -0.35\n        p: 0.09\n      bn:\n        rho: -0.12\n        p: 0.58\n      am:\n        rho: 0.14\n        p: 0.52\n      yo:\n        rho: -0.02\n        p: 0.93\n      te:\n        rho: -0.18\n        p: 0.4\n      my:\n        rho: 0.1\n        p: 0.64\n    per_lang_significant_negative_rho_count: 1\n    per_lang_significant_positive_rho_count: 0\n    per_lang_nonmonotonic_count: 13\n    pareto_tradeoff_prevalence: 0.08\n    pareto_depth_transfer_drop_final_layers_pp: 0.6\n    mean_shift_delta_auroc_all: 0.0\n    transfer_conditions_summary:\n      zero_shot:\n        mean_auroc: 0.576\n        std: 0.068\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n      mean_shift:\n        mean_auroc: 0.576\n        std: 0.068\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n      linear_proj_200:\n        mean_auroc: 0.612\n        std: 0.055\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.036\n      fewshot_25:\n        mean_auroc: 0.598\n        std: 0.061\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.022\n      fewshot_100:\n        mean_auroc: 0.625\n        std: 0.049\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.049\n  result_rationale: 'EN best AUROC 0.741 在 worst 范围 [0.72, 0.78] 内——Qwen3-235B 的 22B\n    active parameters 对 correctness signal 的编码不显著优于 7B pilot（0.754），因为 correctness\n    direction 的信号 强度主要由 pretraining data 质量和 MCQA 格式暴露量决定，而非模型 scale。INT4 量化引入 ~1pp\n    额外损耗。\n\n    ZS pass 11/20 (55%) 处于 worst 范围 [8, 13] 中段。MoE routing 导致不同语言被路由到 不同 expert 子集，correctness\n    direction 的跨语言一致性被 expert 分化削弱：pilot 中 Qwen2.5-7B dense 架构的 4/5 pass 不能外推，因为 dense\n    model 的 shared representation 天然更有利于 cross-lingual alignment。低资源语言（am, yo, my）的\n    best ZS AUROC < 0.50，接近 random。\n\n    Global Pareto rho=-0.12 (p=0.078) 仅 marginally significant：depth-transfer tradeoff\n    在 MoE 中不成立，因为 expert routing 在不同深度可以 \"重置\" 语言特异性——L48 的 expert allocation 可能与 L72\n    完全不同，打破了 \"deeper = more specialized\" 的 dense-model 假设。13/20 语言呈现 non-monotonic\n    模式（U形、锯齿形、plateau），这是 MoE 的结构性特征而非噪声。仅 hi 达到 per-language significant negative\n    rho（p=0.046），ko 和 ja 方向反转（deeper helps transfer）。\n\n    Final-layer transfer drop 仅 0.6pp（worst 范围 [0.0, 1.5]），远低于 pilot 的 2-4pp—— 235B\n    MoE 的最深层 expert routing 已经足够 specialized，EN probe 在这些层的 AUROC 提升本身就很小（L88 vs L72\n    仅 +0.3pp EN AUROC），所以 transfer drop 也被压缩。\n\n    Mean-shift ΔAUROC ≡ 0 符合已证明的 rank-invariance。Linear projection +3.6pp 和 few-shot\n    100 +4.9pp 有中等改善，但 significant improvement 仅覆盖 55-65% 的语言。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1a: Qwen3-235B Per-Language Pareto (Depth vs ZS-AUROC Spearman ρ)'\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - best_zs_auroc\n    - best_zs_layer\n    - spearman_rho\n    - p_value\n    - pattern\n    rows:\n    - - zh\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.668\n      - 60\n      - -0.31\n      - 0.14\n      - weak negative\n    - - es\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.675\n      - 56\n      - -0.25\n      - 0.24\n      - n.s.\n    - - fr\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.658\n      - 60\n      - -0.28\n      - 0.18\n      - n.s.\n    - - de\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.649\n      - 52\n      - -0.19\n      - 0.38\n      - n.s.\n    - - ja\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.588\n      - 48\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.4\n      - non-monotonic U-shape\n    - - pt\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.662\n      - 56\n      - -0.22\n      - 0.3\n      - n.s.\n    - - it\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.645\n      - 56\n      - -0.16\n      - 0.46\n      - n.s.\n    - - ar\n      - MID\n      - 0.608\n      - 52\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.82\n      - flat\n    - - hi\n      - MID\n      - 0.567\n      - 44\n      - -0.41\n      - 0.046\n      - significant negative\n    - - ru\n      - MID\n      - 0.621\n      - 56\n      - -0.14\n      - 0.52\n      - n.s.\n    - - ko\n      - MID\n      - 0.591\n      - 48\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.24\n      - inverted—deeper helps\n    - - tr\n      - MID\n      - 0.548\n      - 40\n      - -0.08\n      - 0.71\n      - n.s.\n    - - vi\n      - MID\n      - 0.562\n      - 44\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.68\n      - flat\n    - - th\n      - MID\n      - 0.528\n      - 36\n      - -0.11\n      - 0.61\n      - n.s.\n    - - sw\n      - LOW\n      - 0.518\n      - 36\n      - -0.35\n      - 0.09\n      - marginal negative\n    - - bn\n      - LOW\n      - 0.524\n      - 40\n      - -0.12\n      - 0.58\n      - n.s.\n    - - am\n      - LOW\n      - 0.486\n      - 32\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.52\n      - non-monotonic\n    - - yo\n      - LOW\n      - 0.475\n      - 28\n      - -0.02\n      - 0.93\n      - noisy flat\n    - - te\n      - LOW\n      - 0.502\n      - 36\n      - -0.18\n      - 0.4\n      - n.s.\n    - - my\n      - LOW\n      - 0.468\n      - 32\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.64\n      - non-monotonic\n  - name: 'Table 1b: Qwen3-235B Transfer Conditions Summary (20 langs, EN-optimal\n      layer)'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - mean_auroc\n    - std\n    - delta_vs_zs\n    - significant_improvement_count\n    rows:\n    - - zero-shot\n      - 0.576\n      - 0.068\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - mean-shift\n      - 0.576\n      - 0.068\n      - 0.0\n      - 0/20\n    - - linear_proj_200\n      - 0.612\n      - 0.055\n      - 0.036\n      - 11/20\n    - - fewshot_25\n      - 0.598\n      - 0.061\n      - 0.022\n      - 7/20\n    - - fewshot_100\n      - 0.625\n      - 0.049\n      - 0.049\n      - 13/20\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 1a: EN AUROC vs best ZS AUROC scatter across 24 layers for Qwen3-235B,\n    colored by resource tier. Diffuse cloud without clean Pareto frontier. Non-monotonic\n    language trajectories (ja, ko, am, my) highlighted. Annotation: global ρ=-0.12\n    (p=0.078).\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 1b: ZS AUROC heatmap (language × probed layer). Irregular MoE-specific\n    layer-to-layer variance, no smooth depth gradient. Expert routing artifacts visible\n    as 4-layer-period oscillations.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Qwen3-235B 的 Pareto frontier 远不如 Qwen2.5-7B pilot 清晰。MoE expert routing\n    打破了 dense model 中 depth = specialization 的单调映射。Pilot 的 clear Pareto（L27 EN best\n    但 transfer drops 2-4pp vs L24）是 dense 7B model 的特殊现象。仅 1/20 语言达到 per-language\n    显著性（hi），且部分语言方向反转——depth-transfer tradeoff 不是普遍现象。对 Claim 1 构成 严重挑战：不能声称 Qwen\n    系列存在 consistent Pareto。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama 4 Scout Full Pareto Frontier\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: 'Llama 4 Scout (48 layers, 17B-16E MoE, W4A16), 12 probed layers (every\n    4th), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_best_auroc: 0.718\n    en_best_layer: 40\n    en_auroc_range:\n    - 0.615\n    - 0.718\n    en_best_ece_raw: 0.215\n    zs_pass_count_auroc_gt_058: 9\n    zs_pass_rate: 0.45\n    mean_zs_auroc_all_20: 0.562\n    mean_zs_auroc_drop_vs_en_pp: 15.6\n    best_zs_auroc:\n      zh: 0.648\n      es: 0.655\n      fr: 0.642\n      de: 0.635\n      ja: 0.562\n      pt: 0.648\n      it: 0.631\n      ar: 0.588\n      hi: 0.548\n      ru: 0.608\n      ko: 0.575\n      tr: 0.531\n      vi: 0.558\n      th: 0.515\n      sw: 0.501\n      bn: 0.508\n      am: 0.472\n      yo: 0.458\n      te: 0.491\n      my: 0.452\n    global_spearman_rho_depth_vs_transfer: -0.06\n    global_spearman_p: 0.31\n    per_lang_significant_negative_rho_count: 0\n    per_lang_significant_positive_rho_count: 0\n    per_lang_nonmonotonic_count: 8\n    pareto_tradeoff_prevalence: 0.05\n    pareto_depth_transfer_drop_final_layers_pp: 0.3\n    mean_shift_delta_auroc_all: 0.0\n    transfer_conditions_summary:\n      zero_shot:\n        mean_auroc: 0.562\n        std: 0.065\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n      mean_shift:\n        mean_auroc: 0.562\n        std: 0.065\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n      linear_proj_200:\n        mean_auroc: 0.598\n        std: 0.052\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.036\n      fewshot_25:\n        mean_auroc: 0.584\n        std: 0.058\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.022\n      fewshot_100:\n        mean_auroc: 0.611\n        std: 0.048\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.049\n  result_rationale: 'Llama 4 Scout EN best AUROC 0.718 在 worst 范围低端——active parameters\n    17B 但 16 experts 的稀疏激活使得每个 token 实际使用的参数量有限，correctness signal 在 expert 间被稀释。W4A16\n    量化额外损耗 ~0.5-1pp。\n\n    ZS pass 9/20 (45%)，比 Qwen3 低因为：(1) Llama 4 Scout 的 multilingual pretraining 比例可能低于\n    Qwen3（Qwen 系列历来强调多语言）；(2) 16-expert MoE 的 expert specialization 程度更高，语言间 representation\n    divergence 更大。MVP 中 Llama-3.1-8B dense 的 5/5 pass 不推广——8B dense → Scout MoE 的架构变化比\n    scale change 更根本。\n\n    Global Pareto rho=-0.06 (p=0.31) 完全不显著，0/20 语言 per-language 显著。仅 12 probed layers\n    使 per-language Spearman 功效极低（n=12），但即使考虑 power 问题，effect sizes 也很小 （max |rho|\n    = 0.38）。Scout 的 expert routing 比 Qwen3 更激进（16 experts vs Qwen3 的 设计），导致 depth-transfer\n    关系更加 noisy。\n\n    Final-layer drop 仅 0.3pp——transfer 在 L40-L48 区间几乎 flat，没有 tradeoff 可言。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2a: Llama 4 Scout Per-Language Pareto Spearman ρ'\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - best_zs_auroc\n    - spearman_rho\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - zh\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.648\n      - -0.18\n      - 0.58\n    - - es\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.655\n      - -0.12\n      - 0.71\n    - - fr\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.642\n      - -0.22\n      - 0.49\n    - - de\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.635\n      - -0.08\n      - 0.81\n    - - ja\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.562\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.31\n    - - pt\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.648\n      - -0.15\n      - 0.64\n    - - it\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.631\n      - -0.05\n      - 0.88\n    - - ar\n      - MID\n      - 0.588\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.49\n    - - hi\n      - MID\n      - 0.548\n      - -0.38\n      - 0.22\n    - - ru\n      - MID\n      - 0.608\n      - -0.02\n      - 0.95\n    - - ko\n      - MID\n      - 0.575\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.26\n    - - tr\n      - MID\n      - 0.531\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.81\n    - - vi\n      - MID\n      - 0.558\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.71\n    - - th\n      - MID\n      - 0.515\n      - -0.18\n      - 0.58\n    - - sw\n      - LOW\n      - 0.501\n      - -0.25\n      - 0.43\n    - - bn\n      - LOW\n      - 0.508\n      - -0.08\n      - 0.81\n    - - am\n      - LOW\n      - 0.472\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.95\n    - - yo\n      - LOW\n      - 0.458\n      - -0.12\n      - 0.71\n    - - te\n      - LOW\n      - 0.491\n      - -0.05\n      - 0.88\n    - - my\n      - LOW\n      - 0.452\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.64\n  - name: 'Table 2b: Llama 4 Scout Transfer Conditions Summary'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - mean_auroc\n    - delta_vs_zs\n    - significant_count\n    rows:\n    - - zero-shot\n      - 0.562\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - mean-shift\n      - 0.562\n      - 0.0\n      - 0/20\n    - - linear_proj_200\n      - 0.598\n      - 0.036\n      - 10/20\n    - - fewshot_25\n      - 0.584\n      - 0.022\n      - 6/20\n    - - fewshot_100\n      - 0.611\n      - 0.049\n      - 12/20\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: Llama 4 Scout Pareto scatter, same format as Figure 1a. Cloud 更散乱，\n    global ρ=-0.06 (p=0.31)。ko (+0.35) 和 ja (+0.32) 方向反转于预期。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Llama 4 Scout 确认 MoE 架构的 Pareto 缺失。与 Qwen3 合并看：0 个 MoE 架构在 p<0.05 展现\n    Pareto。MVP 中 Llama-3.1-8B 的弱 Pareto 是 dense 架构特有的。两个 MoE 结合表明 expert routing 是\n    Pareto 缺失的结构性原因，而非偶然。\n\n    '\n- name: Gemma 4 31B Dense Pareto Frontier\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: 'Gemma 4 31B Dense (60 text layers, BF16 无量化), 16 probed layers (every\n    4th + final), 20 languages, 5 transfer conditions. Dense vs MoE 对照。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_best_auroc: 0.755\n    en_best_layer: 52\n    en_auroc_range:\n    - 0.618\n    - 0.755\n    en_best_ece_raw: 0.188\n    zs_pass_count_auroc_gt_058: 12\n    zs_pass_rate: 0.6\n    mean_zs_auroc_all_20: 0.585\n    mean_zs_auroc_drop_vs_en_pp: 17.0\n    best_zs_auroc:\n      zh: 0.682\n      es: 0.691\n      fr: 0.672\n      de: 0.665\n      ja: 0.598\n      pt: 0.678\n      it: 0.658\n      ar: 0.618\n      hi: 0.575\n      ru: 0.635\n      ko: 0.602\n      tr: 0.558\n      vi: 0.572\n      th: 0.538\n      sw: 0.525\n      bn: 0.531\n      am: 0.492\n      yo: 0.481\n      te: 0.508\n      my: 0.475\n    global_spearman_rho_depth_vs_transfer: -0.24\n    global_spearman_p: 0.038\n    per_lang_significant_negative_rho_count: 4\n    per_lang_significant_positive_rho_count: 0\n    per_lang_nonmonotonic_count: 5\n    pareto_tradeoff_prevalence: 0.22\n    pareto_depth_transfer_drop_final_layers_pp: 0.8\n    spearman_depth_vs_transfer_rho_positive_langs: 10\n    transfer_conditions_summary:\n      zero_shot:\n        mean_auroc: 0.585\n        std: 0.063\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n      mean_shift:\n        mean_auroc: 0.585\n        std: 0.063\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.0\n      linear_proj_200:\n        mean_auroc: 0.621\n        std: 0.051\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.036\n      fewshot_25:\n        mean_auroc: 0.607\n        std: 0.057\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.022\n      fewshot_100:\n        mean_auroc: 0.634\n        std: 0.045\n        delta_vs_zs: 0.049\n  result_rationale: 'Gemma 4 31B Dense 是唯一有 marginal Pareto 的架构。Dense 架构没有 expert\n    routing， depth→specialization 映射更单调，因此 global rho=-0.24 (p=0.038) 达到 significance。\n    4/20 语言 per-language 显著（zh, fr, hi, sw）——全部是负 rho（deeper layers = worse transfer），\n    符合 specialization 叙述。\n\n    但这反而增加了叙述复杂性：Pareto 是 architecture-dependent 的（dense 有，MoE 没有）， 无法声称是普遍现象。且 final-layer\n    drop 仅 0.8pp——远低于 pilot 的 2-4pp，因为 31B dense model 的最深层已经足够 expressive，EN probe\n    的边际 AUROC 提升很小（L56→L60 仅 +0.4pp）， 相应 transfer 损失也被压缩。\n\n    EN AUROC 0.755 略高于两个 MoE（因无量化损耗 + BF16 保留更多信号精度），三架构均值 (0.741 + 0.718 + 0.755)/3\n    = 0.738，在 worst 范围 [0.72, 0.78] 内。\n\n    ZS pass 12/20 (60%)——三架构最高，因为 Gemma 4 的 multilingual pretraining 可能 更均衡（Apache\n    2.0 开源模型通常 training data 更 curated），且无量化损耗。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Gemma 4 31B Dense Pareto Summary'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - value\n    rows:\n    - - en_best_auroc\n      - 0.755\n    - - en_best_layer\n      - L52 (87% depth)\n    - - zs_pass_rate\n      - 60% (12/20)\n    - - global_pareto_rho\n      - -0.24 (p=0.038)\n    - - per_lang_significant_rho\n      - 4/20 (zh, fr, hi, sw)\n    - - final_layer_transfer_drop_pp\n      - 0.8\n    - - control_artifact_rate_LOW\n      - 38%\n    - - no_quantization_confound\n      - BF16 — no quantization artifact\n  - name: 'Table 3b: Dense vs MoE Architecture Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - Qwen3 (MoE)\n    - Llama4 (MoE)\n    - Gemma4 (Dense)\n    rows:\n    - - en_best_auroc\n      - 0.741\n      - 0.718\n      - 0.755\n    - - global_pareto_rho\n      - -0.12 (n.s.)\n      - -0.06 (n.s.)\n      - -0.24 (p=0.038)\n    - - per_lang_sig_count\n      - 1/20\n      - 0/20\n      - 4/20\n    - - non_monotonic_langs\n      - 13/20\n      - 8/20\n      - 5/20\n    - - final_layer_drop_pp\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.8\n    - - zs_pass_rate\n      - 55%\n      - 45%\n      - 60%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3a: Gemma 4 Pareto scatter vs Qwen3/Llama4 (3-panel). Gemma shows cleaner\n    negative trend but still substantial scatter. MoE panels show diffuse clouds.\n    Visual comparison highlights dense vs MoE structural difference.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 3b: Per-language Spearman ρ bar chart across 3 architectures. Gemma bars\n    lean negative but most still n.s. MoE bars scattered around zero.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Dense vs MoE 对比是 Gemma 最大的贡献：dense 架构确实有 cleaner depth-transfer 关系， 但\n    effect size 远小于 pilot 预期。三架构综合 pareto_tradeoff_prevalence ≈ 0.12 (12% of lang-arch\n    pairs)，在 worst 范围 [0.05, 0.25] 内。 结论：Pareto 是 architecture-conditional 的，不是 universal\n    finding——这使得 Claim 1 从 \"discovery\" 降级为 \"architecture-dependent observational note\"。\n\n    '\n- name: CaCLR Implementation and Comparative Evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 'CaCLR (L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_MMD), β sweep 3 OOM, α sweep, component\n    ablation, CORAL comparison, high-dim MMD (PCA d=50/100), multi-seed (5 seeds),\n    mixed β criterion. vs 4 baselines, 3 models × 20 langs.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    caclr_mean_delta_auroc_vs_zs: -0.008\n    caclr_langs_improved_of_20: 4\n    caclr_best_beta: none — all β inert or harmful\n    beta_sweep:\n      beta_0.001:\n        mean_delta_auroc: -0.002\n        std: 0.016\n      beta_0.01:\n        mean_delta_auroc: -0.005\n        std: 0.019\n      beta_0.1:\n        mean_delta_auroc: -0.009\n        std: 0.023\n      beta_1.0:\n        mean_delta_auroc: -0.016\n        std: 0.028\n    alpha_sweep:\n      alpha_0.01:\n        delta_auroc: -0.001\n        delta_ece: 0.006\n      alpha_0.1:\n        delta_auroc: -0.004\n        delta_ece: 0.002\n      alpha_1.0:\n        delta_auroc: -0.01\n        delta_ece: -0.001\n      alpha_10.0:\n        delta_auroc: -0.025\n        delta_ece: -0.004\n    component_ablation:\n      bce_only:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.001\n        note: ≈ ZS baseline\n      bce_plus_sbece:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.005\n        note: SB-ECE hurts discrimination\n      bce_plus_mmd_1d:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.004\n        note: 1-D MMD inert/harmful\n      bce_plus_mmd_pca50:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.006\n        note: 50-D MMD also fails\n      bce_plus_mmd_pca100:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.008\n        note: 100-D MMD worse — curse of dimensionality\n      bce_plus_coral:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.005\n        note: CORAL fails — second-order alignment insufficient\n      bce_plus_coral_pca50:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.007\n        note: high-dim CORAL also fails\n      full_caclr:\n        delta_vs_zs: -0.008\n        note: compound degradation\n    multi_seed_std:\n      caclr: 0.003\n      fewshot_25: 0.008\n      fewshot_100: 0.005\n      procrustes: 0.002\n    mixed_beta_criterion_result: 'β selected on zh+sw validation matches English-only\n      selection (β=0.001). No evidence of systematic bias against cross-lingual benefit.\n\n      '\n    five_way_comparison:\n      zero_shot:\n        mean_auroc: 0.574\n        mean_ece: 0.282\n      mean_shift:\n        mean_auroc: 0.574\n        mean_ece: 0.288\n      caclr_best:\n        mean_auroc: 0.566\n        mean_ece: 0.275\n      linear_proj_200:\n        mean_auroc: 0.61\n        mean_ece: 0.245\n      fewshot_25:\n        mean_auroc: 0.596\n        mean_ece: 0.258\n      fewshot_100:\n        mean_auroc: 0.623\n        mean_ece: 0.232\n    implementation_spec:\n      mmd_kernel: Gaussian RBF, bandwidth=median heuristic\n      optimizer: Adam, lr=1e-3, cosine schedule to 1e-5\n      epochs: 50\n      early_stopping: patience=10 on held-out English BCE loss\n      initialization: from standard LR solution\n      batch_size: 256\n      mmd_items: same items as BCE (probe_train 70% split)\n      parallel_set_size_range:\n      - 618\n      - 2852\n  result_rationale: 'CaCLR 失败的根本原因链：\n\n    (1) 1-D MMD 结构性限制：probe logit 是标量，MMD 只能 match 两个 1-D 分布的 marginal。 即使 marginal\n    被 match，EN 和 target 的 conditional distributions P(logit|correct) vs P(logit|incorrect)\n    仍然不同——Zhao et al. (2019) 的理论预测在此得到验证。β 越大，logits 被拉向无区分性的 marginal match，discrimination\n    下降。\n\n    (2) High-dim MMD (PCA d=50/100) 同样失败：curse of dimensionality 使得 Gaussian RBF kernel\n    在 50-100 维空间的 MMD estimate 方差极大，有效样本量不足（probe_train ~2000 samples 对 100 维 MMD\n    来说 severely underpowered）。d=100 比 d=50 更差，证实这一解释。\n\n    (3) CORAL 也失败：second-order alignment（match mean + covariance）比 MMD 更受 conditional\n    distribution mismatch 的影响——对齐 marginal moments 不能修复 correctness signal 的 conditional\n    structure 差异。CORAL 在 domain adaptation 中成功的条件是 covariate shift （P(X) changes,\n    P(Y|X) stable），但 cross-lingual correctness probing 违反这一条件 （P(correct|representation)\n    在不同语言中不同）。\n\n    (4) Component ablation 证实每个额外 loss 都是 net negative：BCE-only retrain ≈ ZS baseline（LR\n    solution 初始化后 Adam 微调不改变 optimum），每加一项都引入额外 noise 而 无 signal。CaCLR 不是超参选择问题而是方法论层面的失败。\n\n    (5) Multi-seed 结果稳定（std=0.003），排除了 single-seed 偶然性。Mixed β criterion 排除了 β selection\n    对 cross-lingual benefit 的系统性偏见。\n\n    综合：distributional matching 路径（MMD + CORAL，low-dim + high-dim）被全面关闭。 Linear projection\n    和 few-shot 显著优于 CaCLR，因为它们直接利用 target-language 结构 信息而非试图间接 match distributions。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4a: CaCLR β Sweep (3 architectures × 20 langs, EN-optimal layer)'\n    columns:\n    - beta\n    - mean_auroc\n    - delta_vs_zs\n    - pct_improved\n    - pct_harmed\n    rows:\n    - - 0.001\n      - 0.572\n      - -0.002\n      - 30%\n      - 42%\n    - - 0.01\n      - 0.569\n      - -0.005\n      - 25%\n      - 52%\n    - - 0.1\n      - 0.565\n      - -0.009\n      - 18%\n      - 62%\n    - - 1.0\n      - 0.558\n      - -0.016\n      - 12%\n      - 75%\n  - name: 'Table 4b: Distributional Matching Comprehensive Ablation'\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - dimensionality\n    - mean_delta_auroc\n    - note\n    rows:\n    - - MMD (logit)\n      - 1-D\n      - -0.004\n      - marginal match, no conditional alignment\n    - - MMD (PCA-50)\n      - 50-D\n      - -0.006\n      - underpowered MMD in 50-D\n    - - MMD (PCA-100)\n      - 100-D\n      - -0.008\n      - curse of dimensionality\n    - - CORAL (logit)\n      - 1-D\n      - -0.005\n      - second-order alignment insufficient\n    - - CORAL (PCA-50)\n      - 50-D\n      - -0.007\n      - covariance match fails\n    - - Linear projection\n      - full-D Procrustes\n      - 0.036\n      - learns subspace rotation directly\n  - name: 'Table 4c: 5-Way Transfer Comparison (3 arch × 20 langs)'\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - mean_auroc\n    - mean_ece\n    - delta_auroc_vs_zs\n    - win_rate_vs_zs\n    rows:\n    - - zero-shot\n      - 0.574\n      - 0.282\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - mean-shift\n      - 0.574\n      - 0.288\n      - 0.0\n      - 0%\n    - - CaCLR (best)\n      - 0.566\n      - 0.275\n      - -0.008\n      - 20%\n    - - linear_proj_200\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.245\n      - 0.036\n      - 70%\n    - - fewshot_25\n      - 0.596\n      - 0.258\n      - 0.022\n      - 52%\n    - - fewshot_100\n      - 0.623\n      - 0.232\n      - 0.049\n      - 75%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4a: β sweep curve showing monotonic decrease in mean AUROC. Shaded 95%\n    CI all below or crossing zero-shot baseline. Separate lines for MMD-1D, MMD-50D,\n    MMD-100D, CORAL showing all fail.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 4b: Per-language ΔAUROC bars at best β=0.001. Most bars negative. Only\n    4 HIGH-resource languages show marginal positive Δ within noise margin.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 4c: Distributional matching ablation (MMD vs CORAL × dimensionality).\n    All configurations below zero-shot. Linear projection (rightmost) is the only\n    positive method. Clean visual separation between distribution-matching (all negative)\n    and structure-learning (linear projection, positive).\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'CaCLR 的全面 negative result 是 worst tier 的核心贡献之一。关键升级：CORAL + high-dim\n    MMD 将 scope 从 \"MMD fails\" 扩展为 \"distributional matching path is closed\"。这比仅报告 1-D\n    MMD 失败有力得多——reviewer 无法反驳说 \"换个 kernel/提高维度就行\"。 Distributional matching ablation\n    table (Table 4b) 是该 claim 的 anchor evidence。 CKA subspace 解释也不成立（plan_011），所以\n    geometric rationalization 也失败—— 不仅方法失败，elegant 解释也失败。但完整的 implementation spec\n    + sweep + ablation 确保 reproducibility，使 negative result 可信。\n\n    '\n- name: Difficulty-Controlled Decomposition Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 'IRT difficulty probes → project out difficulty direction → retrain\n    correctness probes on residuals → evaluate transfer. 10 representative languages\n    × 8 representative layers × 3 models. Random-direction control.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    decomp_transfer_improvement_pp: 0.2\n    decomp_transfer_improvement_range:\n    - -0.8\n    - 1.2\n    random_direction_control_delta_pp: -0.1\n    random_direction_control_range:\n    - -1.0\n    - 0.8\n    decomp_vs_random_paired_test_p: 0.38\n    difficulty_probe_r2: 0.28\n    decomp_langs_showing_clean_separation: 2\n    per_tier_results:\n      HIGH:\n        mean_delta_pp: 0.3\n        significant: 0/4\n        clean_separation: 1\n      MID:\n        mean_delta_pp: 0.1\n        significant: 0/3\n        clean_separation: 1\n      LOW:\n        mean_delta_pp: -0.2\n        significant: 0/3\n        clean_separation: 0\n  result_rationale: 'Decomposition 在 worst tier 无实质效果，两个层面的失败：\n\n    (1) Difficulty direction 在 LLM representation 中编码不够 linear/集中——IRT difficulty\n    probe R²=0.28（低），意味着 linear projection 只捕获了 difficulty variance 的 28%。 剩余 72%\n    的 difficulty 信息分布在 correctness direction 也占据的子空间中——两者高度 纠缠，projecting out 28%\n    的 difficulty 同时损坏了部分 correctness signal。\n\n    (2) Random-direction control 产生同量级效果（paired test p=0.38），这是 worst tier 的 killer\n    finding：观察到的微小 delta 主要来自 dimensionality reduction 效应 （投影去除任意方向都会改变 probe 性能 ≈\n    同量级），而非 difficulty-specific 信号去除。\n\n    2/10 语言 \"clean separation\"（zh, ko）可能是 type-I error 在 10 次检验中的自然出现率。 LOW tier 3\n    语言全部 negative delta——它们的 difficulty 和 capability 信号本身就很弱， 投影去除任何方向只会损失信息。\n\n    结论：transfer degradation 不能分解为 difficulty-shared + capability-specific 两个可操作的 component——Claim\n    2 被否定，decomposition 从 standalone claim 降级。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: Difficulty Decomposition Ablation (3 models mean)'\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - original_zs\n    - after_proj\n    - delta_pp\n    - random_ctrl_delta_pp\n    - paired_p\n    rows:\n    - - zh\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.666\n      - 0.67\n      - 0.4\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.45\n    - - es\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.674\n      - 0.676\n      - 0.2\n      - -0.1\n      - 0.58\n    - - fr\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.657\n      - 0.66\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.82\n    - - de\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.652\n      - 0.2\n      - -0.2\n      - 0.41\n    - - hi\n      - MID\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.565\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.91\n    - - ru\n      - MID\n      - 0.621\n      - 0.622\n      - 0.1\n      - -0.2\n      - 0.52\n    - - ko\n      - MID\n      - 0.589\n      - 0.598\n      - 0.9\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.08\n    - - tr\n      - MID\n      - 0.546\n      - 0.54\n      - -0.6\n      - -0.4\n      - 0.65\n    - - sw\n      - LOW\n      - 0.515\n      - 0.51\n      - -0.5\n      - -0.3\n      - 0.71\n    - - bn\n      - LOW\n      - 0.521\n      - 0.519\n      - -0.2\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.68\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 5: Paired bar chart of ΔAUROC after difficulty projection (blue) vs random-direction\n    projection (gray). Error bars = bootstrap 95% CI. All CIs overlap; no language\n    shows meaningful separation. Vertical dashed line at 0.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Decomposition null result 与 random control 不可区分。Claim 2 被否定。 在 worst\n    tier paper 中这成为另一条被关闭的路径，但不需要大篇幅—— 1 table + 1 figure 在 Section 5.2 用 1 paragraph\n    报告即可。\n\n    '\n- name: Cross-Lingual Orthogonality Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 'Correctness-confidence cosine similarity, 20 languages × 2 architectures\n    (Qwen3 + Llama4), resource-tier 和 language family 分析.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mean_cosine_high: 0.035\n    mean_cosine_mid: 0.062\n    mean_cosine_low: 0.108\n    std_cosine_low: 0.078\n    cosine_range_all:\n    - 0.012\n    - 0.192\n    architecture_agreement_rate: 0.65\n    outlier_langs:\n    - am\n    - yo\n    - my\n  result_rationale: 'Orthogonality 在 HIGH resource 语言成立（cosine < 0.05），复现 Miao & Ungar\n    (2026)。 但 LOW resource 的 cosine 显著升高且方差大（mean 0.108, std 0.078）——原因不是真正的 非正交结构，而是两个\n    probe 都更 noisy：correctness probe selectivity 低（plan_013 控制 任务发现），confidence probe\n    同样缺乏区分性信号，两个 noisy direction 的 cosine 自然 偏离 0。Architecture 一致性仅 65%：7/20 语言两架构给出矛盾信号——可能反映不同\n    MoE routing 对 confidence 编码方式的影响。\n\n    作为已降级的 subsection，这些结果增加复杂性但无 clean takeaway。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: Correctness-Confidence Orthogonality by Resource Tier'\n    columns:\n    - tier\n    - n_langs\n    - mean_cosine\n    - std\n    - min\n    - max\n    - arch_agreement\n    rows:\n    - - HIGH\n      - 7\n      - 0.035\n      - 0.012\n      - 0.012\n      - 0.052\n      - 6/7\n    - - MID\n      - 7\n      - 0.062\n      - 0.025\n      - 0.035\n      - 0.095\n      - 5/7\n    - - LOW\n      - 6\n      - 0.108\n      - 0.078\n      - 0.042\n      - 0.192\n      - 2/6\n    - - ALL\n      - 20\n      - 0.065\n      - 0.055\n      - 0.012\n      - 0.192\n      - 13/20\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S1 (appendix): Box plot of cosine similarity by resource tier, faceted\n    by architecture. LOW tier shows higher median and wider spread. Dashed line at\n    cosine=0.10.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Orthogonality 作为 subsection 贡献有限。LOW tier 的高 cosine 可能是 probe noise 而非真\n    non-orthogonality（control task artifact rate 42% in LOW tier）。 简化为 1 paragraph\n    + 1 table 在 supporting evidence 小节。\n\n    '\n- name: Probe Complexity Comparison\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 'Logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP, EN accuracy + cross-lingual transfer\n    degradation + calibration, 3 models × 20 languages.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    en_auroc_lr_mean: 0.738\n    en_auroc_mlp_mean: 0.752\n    mlp_en_advantage_pp: 1.4\n    zs_transfer_degradation_lr_pp: 15.8\n    zs_transfer_degradation_mlp_pp: 19.4\n    mlp_transfer_disadvantage_pp: 3.6\n    lr_better_for_transfer_pct: 0.72\n    ece_lr_mean: 0.238\n    ece_mlp_mean: 0.252\n  result_rationale: 'MLP 更高 capacity → EN +1.4pp，但跨语言 transfer degradation 更大（-19.4%\n    vs -15.8%）， 符合 \"linear probes transfer better\" 假设。在 worst tier 下 effect size 中等\n    （Cohen''s d ≈ 0.35），72% 语言支持 LR。部分 HIGH resource 语言中 MLP 额外 capacity 弥补了 transfer\n    loss。结论方向正确但不 dramatic——LR 作为默认 choice 被 confirm， MLP 结果放 appendix。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S2: Probe Complexity Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - logistic_regression\n    - mlp_2layer\n    - delta\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - EN AUROC\n      - 0.738\n      - 0.752\n      - 0.014\n      - 0.006\n    - - ZS degradation\n      - 15.8%\n      - 19.4%\n      - +3.6pp\n      - 0.018\n    - - ZS AUROC\n      - 0.621\n      - 0.608\n      - -0.013\n      - 0.032\n    - - EN ECE\n      - 0.238\n      - 0.252\n      - 0.014\n      - 0.058\n    - - LR better for transfer\n      - 72%\n      - 28%\n      - —\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S2 (appendix): Layer-wise EN AUROC for LR vs MLP (upper panel) paired\n    with ZS AUROC (lower panel). MLP advantage grows with EN depth; LR advantage grows\n    with transfer depth.\n\n    '\n  analysis: '方向符合预期但 effect size 中等。在 worst tier 的 high-artifact 环境下，probe complexity\n    不是主要问题。保持 LR 默认，appendix 报告 MLP 对比。\n\n    '\n- name: Additional Benchmark Evaluation (Belebele + MMLU-ProX)\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'Best probes + all transfer conditions on Belebele (20 langs) and MMLU-ProX\n    (20 langs). Cross-benchmark generalization test.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    belebele_zs_pass_rate: 0.45\n    belebele_mean_zs_auroc: 0.545\n    belebele_vs_globalmmlu_spearman: 0.71\n    belebele_mean_delta_vs_globalmmlu: -0.029\n    mmlupx_zs_pass_rate: 0.55\n    mmlupx_mean_zs_auroc: 0.565\n    mmlupx_vs_globalmmlu_spearman: 0.79\n    caclr_belebele_delta: -0.015\n    caclr_mmlupx_delta: -0.009\n    linear_proj_belebele_delta: 0.028\n    linear_proj_mmlupx_delta: 0.033\n  result_rationale: 'Belebele (reading comprehension) 与 MCQA correctness probing 的\n    task mismatch 导致更低 pass rate。Correctness probe 在 GlobalMMLU 上学到的 \"correct answer\"\n    signal 部分依赖于 MCQA-specific format cues（如选项长度、academic domain structure），这些 在 Belebele\n    的 reading comprehension 中缺失。MMLU-ProX 与 GlobalMMLU 更接近（同为 知识 MCQA），correlation\n    更高。\n\n    CaCLR 在 out-of-distribution data 上更差——distribution mismatch 被放大。 Linear projection\n    仍正但幅度缩小。\n\n    Worst tier 意味着 generalization 弱化了已经微弱的 positive findings， 暗示 correctness probing\n    可能 MCQA-specific。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S3: Cross-Benchmark Generalization'\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - zs_pass_rate\n    - mean_zs_auroc\n    - caclr_Δ\n    - linproj_Δ\n    - corr_vs_globalmmlu\n    rows:\n    - - GlobalMMLU\n      - 57%\n      - 0.574\n      - -0.008\n      - 0.036\n      - —\n    - - Belebele\n      - 45%\n      - 0.545\n      - -0.015\n      - 0.028\n      - 0.71\n    - - MMLU-ProX\n      - 55%\n      - 0.565\n      - -0.009\n      - 0.033\n      - 0.79\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S3 (appendix): Per-language ZS AUROC scatter: GlobalMMLU vs Belebele and\n    GlobalMMLU vs MMLU-ProX. Moderate positive correlation with visible deviations\n    for low-resource languages.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark generalization moderate。Belebele 低 performance 暗示 correctness\n    probing 对 task format 敏感——在 worst tier paper 中增加一层 caveat。 放 appendix 作为 generalization\n    check。\n\n    '\n- name: Quantization Validation Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '(a) W4A16 vs FP16 for Llama 4 Scout, 5 representative layers, 5% data\n    subset; (b) INT4 vs FP16 for Qwen3-235B, 5 representative layers, 5% data subset.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    llama_w4a16_vs_fp16:\n      mean_delta_auroc: 0.008\n      max_delta_auroc: 0.016\n      rank_preservation: 0.92\n    qwen_int4_vs_fp16:\n      mean_delta_auroc: 0.011\n      max_delta_auroc: 0.021\n      rank_preservation: 0.89\n    problematic_layers: 2\n    gemma_note: BF16, no quantization — serves as quantization-free control\n  result_rationale: 'Quantization artifacts 不灾难性但 non-negligible。深层（80-95% depth）受影响最大，\n    因为 correctness signal 在这些层最集中，而高频/低方差的 correctness direction 对 quantization noise\n    更敏感。INT4 (Qwen) 比 W4A16 (Llama) 更aggressive，所以 delta 更大。Rank preservation 88-92%\n    意味着 per-language ranking 大体保持但不完美。\n\n    Worst tier 下这创造一个 caveat：深层 probe 结论 potentially 受量化影响。 Gemma 4 BF16 无量化，提供了 quantization-free\n    的 architecture 数据点。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S4: Quantization Validation'\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - quant\n    - layer_pct\n    - fp16_auroc\n    - quant_auroc\n    - delta\n    - rank_ok\n    rows:\n    - - Llama4\n      - W4A16\n      - 20%\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.647\n      - -0.003\n      - ✓\n    - - Llama4\n      - W4A16\n      - 40%\n      - 0.675\n      - 0.668\n      - -0.007\n      - ✓\n    - - Llama4\n      - W4A16\n      - 60%\n      - 0.698\n      - 0.688\n      - -0.01\n      - ✓\n    - - Llama4\n      - W4A16\n      - 80%\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.696\n      - -0.014\n      - ✗ (2 swaps)\n    - - Llama4\n      - W4A16\n      - 95%\n      - 0.715\n      - 0.699\n      - -0.016\n      - ✗ (3 swaps)\n    - - Qwen3\n      - INT4\n      - 20%\n      - 0.628\n      - 0.623\n      - -0.005\n      - ✓\n    - - Qwen3\n      - INT4\n      - 40%\n      - 0.672\n      - 0.662\n      - -0.01\n      - ✓\n    - - Qwen3\n      - INT4\n      - 60%\n      - 0.705\n      - 0.692\n      - -0.013\n      - ✗ (1 swap)\n    - - Qwen3\n      - INT4\n      - 80%\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.714\n      - -0.016\n      - ✗ (3 swaps)\n    - - Qwen3\n      - INT4\n      - 95%\n      - 0.741\n      - 0.72\n      - -0.021\n      - ✗ (4 swaps)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S4 (appendix): Layer-wise quantization delta for both models. Monotonic\n    increase in delta with depth. Horizontal dashed line at 1.5pp threshold.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Quantization 在深层引入 1-2pp 偏差，不改变主要 negative result 结论 （negative results\n    不依赖精确数值），但增加 limitations 内容。 Gemma BF16 作为 quantization-free control 点使得 Gemma\n    的结果最可信。\n\n    '\n- name: CKA Cross-Lingual Representation Similarity Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 'CKA (linear kernel) EN vs target, all probed layers, 20 langs × 3\n    models. Simpson''s Paradox full-scale validation. Partial correlation controlling\n    for depth. Same-layer cross-language analysis. Subspace angle analysis.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    simpson_paradox_confirmed_of_3_arch: 0\n    partial_correlations:\n      qwen3:\n        rho: 0.11\n        p: 0.28\n        bootstrap_ci:\n        - -0.08\n        - 0.29\n      llama4:\n        rho: 0.06\n        p: 0.45\n        bootstrap_ci:\n        - -0.12\n        - 0.24\n      gemma4:\n        rho: 0.16\n        p: 0.09\n        bootstrap_ci:\n        - -0.02\n        - 0.33\n    raw_correlations:\n      qwen3:\n        rho: -0.32\n        p: <0.001\n      llama4:\n        rho: -0.38\n        p: <0.001\n      gemma4:\n        rho: -0.29\n        p: <0.001\n    same_layer_cross_lang_analysis:\n      qwen3_significant_layers: 2/24\n      llama4_significant_layers: 0/12\n      gemma4_significant_layers: 1/16\n      median_rho: 0.14\n    subspace_angle:\n      high_tier_range_deg:\n      - 15\n      - 38\n      mid_tier_range_deg:\n      - 28\n      - 52\n      low_tier_range_deg:\n      - 42\n      - 65\n      consistency_across_layers: low — within-language angle std 8-15° across layers\n    pilot_replication:\n      llama_pilot_rho: 0.41\n      llama_fullscale_rho: 0.06\n      verdict: pilot artifact confirmed\n  result_rationale: '这是 worst tier 的 defining falsification。\n\n    5 语言 pilot 的 Simpson''s Paradox 被 20 语言全量数据否定：\n\n    (1) Llama partial rho 从 +0.41 (p=0.006) 骤降至 +0.06 (p=0.45)。原因：pilot 的 5 语言 恰好\n    overrepresented CKA-transfer 相关性最强的语言（zh, ar 有高 CKA + 低 degradation）， 排除了关系最弱的语言。15\n    种新增语言中 MID/LOW tier 的 CKA 模式与 pilot 语言截然不同—— 这些语言的 CKA 虽然也随 depth 下降，但下降斜率和 transfer\n    degradation 之间没有一致的 within-layer 关系。\n\n    (2) Qwen3 rho=+0.11 (p=0.28) 在 pilot 就不显著（+0.18, p=0.274），全量数据只是确认。 Gemma4 rho=+0.16\n    (p=0.09) 是最接近显著的，但 bootstrap CI 跨零（[-0.02, 0.33]）， 不能依赖。\n\n    (3) Same-layer cross-language analysis（n=20 per layer，最强检验）：median rho=0.14， 仅\n    3/52 层 significant——CKA 在 within-layer 水平几乎无预测力。在同一层中，不同语言 的 CKA 差异巨大但 transfer\n    AUROC 差异不 track CKA。\n\n    (4) Subspace angle analysis 否定 \"correctness direction is a robust language-agnostic\n    subspace\"：HIGH tier 15-38°（不是近乎平行），LOW tier 42-65°（近乎 orthogonal）。 Angle 在同一语言的不同层之间也有\n    8-15° 的标准差——correctness direction 不仅跨语言 不一致，在同一语言内也随 depth 漂移。\n\n    结论：CKA 不提供超越 depth 的解释力。从 \"geometric analysis\" 降级为 \"suggestive correlation\"——仅保留\n    CKA heatmap 作为 descriptive visualization。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 7a: Simpson''s Paradox Full-Scale Validation'\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - raw_rho\n    - raw_p\n    - partial_rho\n    - partial_p\n    - pilot_rho\n    - pilot_p\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-235B\n      - -0.32\n      - <0.001\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.28\n      - +0.18 (n.s.)\n      - 0.274\n      - n.s. confirmed\n    - - Llama4-Scout\n      - -0.38\n      - <0.001\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.45\n      - +0.41 (sig.)\n      - 0.006\n      - pilot artifact\n    - - Gemma4-31B\n      - -0.29\n      - <0.001\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.09\n      - N/A\n      - N/A\n      - marginal, CI spans 0\n  - name: 'Table 7b: Same-Layer Cross-Language CKA-Transfer Correlation'\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - total_layers\n    - significant_layers\n    - median_rho\n    - best_layer_rho\n    - best_p\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3\n      - 24\n      - 2/24\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.4\n      - 0.078\n    - - Llama4\n      - 12\n      - 0/12\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.23\n    - - Gemma4\n      - 16\n      - 1/16\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.44\n      - 0.052\n  - name: 'Table 7c: Subspace Angle (Correctness Direction, EN vs Target, at ~60%\n      depth)'\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - qwen3_angle\n    - llama4_angle\n    - gemma4_angle\n    rows:\n    - - zh\n      - HIGH\n      - 18°\n      - 24°\n      - 16°\n    - - es\n      - HIGH\n      - 15°\n      - 20°\n      - 14°\n    - - ja\n      - HIGH\n      - 35°\n      - 42°\n      - 32°\n    - - ar\n      - MID\n      - 32°\n      - 40°\n      - 30°\n    - - hi\n      - MID\n      - 38°\n      - 46°\n      - 35°\n    - - ko\n      - MID\n      - 28°\n      - 36°\n      - 26°\n    - - tr\n      - MID\n      - 45°\n      - 52°\n      - 42°\n    - - sw\n      - LOW\n      - 52°\n      - 58°\n      - 48°\n    - - bn\n      - LOW\n      - 48°\n      - 55°\n      - 45°\n    - - am\n      - LOW\n      - 62°\n      - 65°\n      - 58°\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 6a: CKA heatmap (language × layer) for 3 models. Shows CKA decline with\n    depth but no clear correspondence to transfer patterns. Color-coded annotations\n    marking same-layer significant correlations (rare).\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 6b: Partial residual scatter (CKA residualized on depth vs transfer AUROC\n    residualized on depth) for 3 models. Diffuse clouds with no visible trend.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 6c: Subspace angle violin plot by resource tier across 3 architectures.\n    Clear tier gradient but HIGH tier also 15-38° range, undermining \"language-agnostic\n    subspace\" claim. LOW tier near orthogonal.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'CKA 的全面失败从 pilot 的 Simpson''s Paradox 标杆发现降级为 \"depth confound 在 raw correlation\n    中占主导，controlling 后无 signal\"。Subspace angle 否定了论文的 前提假设：\"correctness direction\n    是 robust language-agnostic subspace\" 不成立。 CKA 框架从解释性分析降级为描述性可视化——保留 heatmap 但不承载因果叙述。\n    3 架构 0/3 Simpson''s Paradox confirmed，在 worst 范围 [0, 1] 内。\n\n    '\n- name: Linear Projection Sensitivity Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 'Procrustes alignment with 10/20/50/100/200 parallel pairs. 3 models\n    × 5 representative layers × 20 languages.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    linear_proj_delta_over_zs_low_resource_pp: 2.8\n    linear_proj_saturation_pairs_mean: 135\n    saturation_by_tier:\n      HIGH:\n        pairs_95pct: 62\n        range:\n        - 38\n        - 92\n      MID:\n        pairs_95pct: 118\n        range:\n        - 72\n        - 158\n      LOW:\n        pairs_95pct: 175\n        range:\n        - 140\n        - 198\n    sample_efficiency_curve:\n      10_pairs:\n        mean_auroc: 0.552\n        pct_of_200: 66%\n      20_pairs:\n        mean_auroc: 0.571\n        pct_of_200: 78%\n      50_pairs:\n        mean_auroc: 0.592\n        pct_of_200: 89%\n      100_pairs:\n        mean_auroc: 0.605\n        pct_of_200: 96%\n      200_pairs:\n        mean_auroc: 0.61\n        pct_of_200: 100%\n    procrustes_reversal:\n      helps_below_zs: < 0.53 (mostly helps)\n      hurts_above_zs: '> 0.62 (mostly hurts)'\n      inconsistent_zone:\n      - 0.53\n      - 0.62\n      note: threshold varies ±0.08 across languages — no single reliable cutoff\n  result_rationale: 'Worst tier 下 linear projection 需 100-135 pairs 达到 95% performance（非\n    50）：\n\n    (1) Subspace angle 在 worst tier 更大更不一致（plan_011），Procrustes 需更多数据 稳定 rotation\n    matrix 估计——50 pairs 在高维空间 rank-deficient。\n\n    (2) LOW resource 语言的 parallel pairs 翻译质量低 → activation noise → 需更多 pairs average\n    out noise。HIGH tier 62 pairs（翻译精确，subspace angle 小）vs LOW tier 175 pairs（翻译 noisy，subspace\n    angle 大）。\n\n    (3) Effect reversal threshold language-specific：inconsistent zone [0.53, 0.62]\n    意味着同一 ZS AUROC 值下不同语言可能被帮助或伤害。例如 ja (HIGH, ZS=0.588) 被 帮助但 ko (MID, ZS=0.589)\n    被伤害——差异来自 subspace angle 和翻译质量的交互作用。 无法给出单一可操作阈值——practitioner recommendation\n    弱化为 \"ZS < 0.50 大概率有益， > 0.65 大概率有害，中间区间需 held-out validation\"。\n\n    低资源语言 delta +2.8pp（worst 范围 [1, 4] 内），仍是唯一可行的 label-free 方案。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8a: Linear Projection Sample Efficiency (3 arch × 20 langs)'\n    columns:\n    - n_pairs\n    - mean_auroc\n    - pct_of_200\n    - std\n    - significant_pct\n    rows:\n    - - 10\n      - 0.552\n      - 66%\n      - 0.062\n      - 22%\n    - - 20\n      - 0.571\n      - 78%\n      - 0.055\n      - 38%\n    - - 50\n      - 0.592\n      - 89%\n      - 0.049\n      - 52%\n    - - 100\n      - 0.605\n      - 96%\n      - 0.044\n      - 65%\n    - - 200\n      - 0.61\n      - 100%\n      - 0.042\n      - 70%\n  - name: 'Table 8b: Pairs to 95% by Resource Tier'\n    columns:\n    - tier\n    - mean\n    - min\n    - max\n    - std\n    rows:\n    - - HIGH\n      - 62\n      - 38\n      - 92\n      - 20\n    - - MID\n      - 118\n      - 72\n      - 158\n      - 32\n    - - LOW\n      - 175\n      - 140\n      - 198\n      - 25\n  - name: 'Table 8c: Procrustes Effect Direction (200 pairs, selected languages)'\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - zs_auroc\n    - linproj_auroc\n    - delta\n    - effect\n    rows:\n    - - am\n      - LOW\n      - 0.483\n      - 0.508\n      - 0.025\n      - helps\n    - - yo\n      - LOW\n      - 0.468\n      - 0.494\n      - 0.026\n      - helps\n    - - sw\n      - LOW\n      - 0.511\n      - 0.528\n      - 0.017\n      - helps\n    - - tr\n      - MID\n      - 0.544\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.016\n      - helps\n    - - hi\n      - MID\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.568\n      - 0.008\n      - marginal\n    - - vi\n      - MID\n      - 0.563\n      - 0.562\n      - -0.001\n      - neutral\n    - - ko\n      - MID\n      - 0.589\n      - 0.582\n      - -0.007\n      - hurts\n    - - ar\n      - MID\n      - 0.606\n      - 0.598\n      - -0.008\n      - hurts\n    - - ru\n      - MID\n      - 0.622\n      - 0.61\n      - -0.012\n      - hurts\n    - - es\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.674\n      - 0.654\n      - -0.02\n      - hurts\n    - - ja\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.588\n      - 0.596\n      - 0.008\n      - helps (despite HIGH)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 7a: Saturation curves faceted by resource tier, 95% threshold marked.\n    Per-language thin lines show within-tier variance. HIGH saturates early, LOW late.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 7b: ZS AUROC (x) vs ΔAUROC (y) scatter. Rough negative trend but wide\n    scatter band. Shaded inconsistent zone [0.53, 0.62] where both ± deltas occur.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Linear projection 是唯一可行 label-free 方案但实用性弱化：需 100+ pairs（非 50）， effect\n    reversal threshold inconsistent。Paper 给出条件性 recommendation： \"ZS < 0.50 大概率有益,\n    > 0.65 大概率有害, 中间需 validation\"—— 比预期的 clean threshold 弱得多，但对 practitioners 仍有指导价值。\n\n    '\n- name: Probing Control Tasks — Cross-Lingual Extension\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 'Hewitt & Liang control tasks extended to 20 languages × all probed\n    layers × 3 models. Selectivity analysis. Multiple selectivity thresholds (0.03,\n    0.05, 0.10). (builds on completed plan_013 EN-only results)\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    cross_lingual_artifact_rate_pct: 35\n    artifact_by_tier:\n      HIGH:\n        rate: 15%\n        selectivity_mean: 0.195\n      MID:\n        rate: 31%\n        selectivity_mean: 0.138\n      LOW:\n        rate: 42%\n        selectivity_mean: 0.082\n    control_task_selectivity_deep_layers: 0.16\n    selectivity_vs_zs_auroc_rho: 0.65\n    threshold_sensitivity:\n      threshold_003:\n        artifact_rate: 42%\n      threshold_005:\n        artifact_rate: 35%\n      threshold_010:\n        artifact_rate: 24%\n    worst_combos:\n    - 'am: selectivity 0.004 at EN-opt layer'\n    - 'yo: selectivity 0.005 at EN-opt layer'\n    - 'my: selectivity 0.006 at EN-opt layer'\n    - 'sw: selectivity 0.008 at EN-opt layer'\n    mid_resource_surprise:\n      tr:\n        selectivity_at_enopt: 0.031\n      th:\n        selectivity_at_enopt: 0.028\n      vi:\n        selectivity_at_enopt: 0.042\n  result_rationale: 'Cross-lingual artifact rate 35% (overall) 是 worst tier 最强贡献。\n\n    LOW tier 42% artifact rate 的原因：am, yo, my, te 等语言在 LLM pretraining 中 极度不足（估计 <\n    0.1% token share），这些语言的 representation 缺乏区分性结构—— probe 学到的主要是 capacity artifacts（随机\n    label 也能达到类似 AUROC）。 Selectivity = real_AUROC - permuted_AUROC 对这些语言仅 0.004-0.008，\n    几乎等于 zero information content。\n\n    MID tier 31% artifact rate 是 worst tier 的 signature finding：不仅低资源有问题—— tr (0.031),\n    th (0.028), vi (0.042) 等中资源语言在 shallow/mid layers 也有大量 artifacts。原因：这些语言虽然 pretraining\n    充足，但 correctness-specific signal （区分 \"模型答对/答错\"）在 representation 中的编码弱于语言 identity\n    signal， probe 部分地拟合了 language-specific capacity pattern 而非 correctness。\n\n    HIGH tier 15% artifact rate 主要出现在 shallow layers（0-30% depth）， 与 plan_013 completed\n    results 一致（L0-L16 selectivity < 0.12）。\n\n    Selectivity 与 ZS AUROC 的 rho=0.65 是最尖锐的发现：暗示 cross-lingual probing 文献中许多 \"positive\n    transfer\" 结果可能是 artifacts——高 ZS AUROC 可能部分反映 capacity artifacts 而非 genuine correctness\n    signal transfer。\n\n    首次在 cross-lingual transfer 场景系统性应用 Hewitt & Liang selectivity—— 发现 artifact 问题远比\n    monolingual probing 严重。Field-level implication。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 9a: Cross-Lingual Artifact Rate by Resource Tier (3 models)'\n    columns:\n    - tier\n    - n_langs\n    - artifact_rate_thresh_005\n    - selectivity_mean\n    - selectivity_std\n    rows:\n    - - HIGH\n      - 7\n      - 15%\n      - 0.195\n      - 0.042\n    - - MID\n      - 7\n      - 31%\n      - 0.138\n      - 0.038\n    - - LOW\n      - 6\n      - 42%\n      - 0.082\n      - 0.035\n    - - ALL\n      - 20\n      - 35%\n      - 0.142\n      - 0.058\n  - name: 'Table 9b: Per-Language Selectivity at EN-Optimal Layer (Qwen3)'\n    columns:\n    - lang\n    - tier\n    - real_auroc\n    - permuted_auroc\n    - selectivity\n    - flag\n    rows:\n    - - en\n      - —\n      - 0.741\n      - 0.488\n      - 0.253\n      - ''\n    - - zh\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.668\n      - 0.495\n      - 0.173\n      - ''\n    - - es\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.675\n      - 0.492\n      - 0.183\n      - ''\n    - - fr\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.658\n      - 0.49\n      - 0.168\n      - ''\n    - - de\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.649\n      - 0.486\n      - 0.163\n      - ''\n    - - ja\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.588\n      - 0.501\n      - 0.087\n      - ''\n    - - pt\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.662\n      - 0.489\n      - 0.173\n      - ''\n    - - it\n      - HIGH\n      - 0.645\n      - 0.492\n      - 0.153\n      - ''\n    - - ar\n      - MID\n      - 0.608\n      - 0.496\n      - 0.112\n      - ''\n    - - hi\n      - MID\n      - 0.567\n      - 0.503\n      - 0.064\n      - ⚠\n    - - ru\n      - MID\n      - 0.621\n      - 0.493\n      - 0.128\n      - ''\n    - - ko\n      - MID\n      - 0.591\n      - 0.499\n      - 0.092\n      - ''\n    - - tr\n      - MID\n      - 0.548\n      - 0.517\n      - 0.031\n      - ⚠\n    - - vi\n      - MID\n      - 0.562\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.042\n      - ⚠\n    - - th\n      - MID\n      - 0.528\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.028\n      - ⚠\n    - - sw\n      - LOW\n      - 0.518\n      - 0.51\n      - 0.008\n      - ⚠⚠\n    - - bn\n      - LOW\n      - 0.524\n      - 0.505\n      - 0.019\n      - ⚠⚠\n    - - am\n      - LOW\n      - 0.486\n      - 0.482\n      - 0.004\n      - ⚠⚠\n    - - yo\n      - LOW\n      - 0.475\n      - 0.47\n      - 0.005\n      - ⚠⚠\n    - - te\n      - LOW\n      - 0.502\n      - 0.492\n      - 0.01\n      - ⚠⚠\n    - - my\n      - LOW\n      - 0.468\n      - 0.462\n      - 0.006\n      - ⚠⚠\n  - name: 'Table 9c: Selectivity Threshold Sensitivity'\n    columns:\n    - threshold\n    - overall_artifact_rate\n    - LOW_rate\n    - MID_rate\n    - HIGH_rate\n    rows:\n    - - 0.03\n      - 42%\n      - 52%\n      - 40%\n      - 22%\n    - - 0.05\n      - 35%\n      - 42%\n      - 31%\n      - 15%\n    - - 0.1\n      - 24%\n      - 35%\n      - 22%\n      - 8%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 8a: Selectivity heatmap (language × layer) for Qwen3-235B. Color scale:\n    red (<0.05) → yellow (0.05-0.10) → green (>0.20). Large red region in LOW × shallow\n    layers. MID-resource red patches at moderate depths are the surprise finding.\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 8b: Selectivity vs ZS AUROC scatter across all language-layer-model combinations.\n    Strong positive correlation (ρ=0.65). Annotation: \"Many ''successful'' transfer\n    results fall in the low-selectivity region.\"\n\n    '\n  - 'Figure 8c: Artifact rate by resource tier with bootstrap 95% CI. MID tier CI\n    overlaps substantially with LOW tier — the problem is not confined to low-resource\n    languages.\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Control task finding 是 worst tier paper 的 anchor contribution。>35% artifact\n    rate 波及中资源语言是 field-level 发现：所有跨语言 probing 研究——包括只看中/高资源的—— 都需要 selectivity 检验。Selectivity-AUROC\n    correlation (ρ=0.65) 暗示文献中许多 positive results 可能是 artifacts。首次系统性应用 Hewitt & Liang\n    到 cross-lingual 场景——这个贡献独立于本文其他所有 claims，即使其他全部失败仍足以支撑 EACL findings paper。\n\n    '\n- name: Extended Language Coverage (50+ Languages)\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '从 20 扩展到 50+ 语言 (camera-ready extension)。Leverages GlobalMMLU/Belebele\n    full language sets。P2 priority。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_languages: 52\n    zs_pass_rate_52lang: 0.5\n    artifact_rate_low_expanded: 0.45\n    artifact_rate_mid_expanded: 0.34\n    new_significant_pareto_langs: 2\n    linear_proj_saturation_mean_expanded: 155\n  result_rationale: '扩展到 52 语言后新增大部分是 MID/LOW resource，ZS pass rate 从 57% → 50% 因为新语言\n    skew lower resource。Control artifact rate 在扩展 LOW tier 升至 45% 因为更多极低资源语言纳入。新增语言不改变核心\n    negative results，主要增加 statistical power 和 coverage credibility。Linear projection\n    saturation mean 升至 155 因为 更多 hard languages。\n\n    扩展语言数的主要价值：(1) control task finding 的 scope 更大——\"近半数低资源跨语言 probing 结果是 artifacts\"\n    在 50+ 语言规模下更有说服力；(2) EACL reviewer 可能要求 更多语言的 coverage；(3) 无量化 Gemma 在 52 语言上的数据最可信。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table S5: 52-Language vs 20-Language Summary'\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - 20_lang\n    - 52_lang\n    - delta\n    rows:\n    - - zs_pass_rate\n      - 57%\n      - 50%\n      - -7pp\n    - - artifact_rate_LOW\n      - 42%\n      - 45%\n      - +3pp\n    - - artifact_rate_MID\n      - 31%\n      - 34%\n      - +3pp\n    - - linear_proj_mean_pairs\n      - 135\n      - 155\n      - '+20'\n    - - max_partial_rho\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.14\n      - '-0.02'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure S5 (camera-ready): World map of ZS AUROC at EN-optimal layer with artifact\n    flags. Sub-Saharan Africa and Southeast Asia dominated by artifact flags. Latin-script\n    European cluster relatively clean.\n\n    '\n  analysis: '52 语言扩展服务于 coverage 和 robustness。核心结论不变但 control task finding 更 impactful，linear\n    projection guidance 更 granular（更多语言的 tier classification）。\n\n    '\n","numLines":2287,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2287}}}
